However, don’t make that turn your back away from Discord. I only said the above to warn you in case anything should happen, which I hope not. In that case, you should report and block immediately. To avoid situations like these, I suggest you join servers that have enforced rules and a good staff. Besides that, Discord isn’t all a horrible place. You can meet wonderful people who are the kindest souls ever and meet bunches of people who have a passion for what you like. It’s a great platform to chat and make friends.",5,134.0,mikeidlee,0
us,United States,11789286487,2024-10-02T08:09:30-07:00,Overall really good,"The app is pretty good overall it’s just that sometimes the UI messes up? Whenever I click on a discord notif in-app and I’m in the voice channel text chat, the tab turns all black and I can’t interact with anything unless I restart the app. Then after opening the app, it’ll still say I’m in call. Then whenever I’m in call, the app will randomly restart, which would be fine if it didn’t mute my friends upon automatically rejoining. (I can see their mic indicator go off but I can’t hear anything they’re saying.) I usually have to restart and rejoin the app again after this happens. Thankfully this next one has only happened twice, but I’ve been kicked from call. I sometimes stay on vc with my friends to help me sleep and I noticed in the morning that I’m not in call anymore which is odd cuz I didn’t close the app nor did anyone kick me out. Not sure if anyone else has had the same experience though. 

Again, great app. It just gets a little inconvenient at times, but still manageable and will continue to use the app either way.",4,249.0,Beep beepp,0
us,United States,10709231503,2023-12-17T13:09:00-07:00,December 2023 Update,"I’ve used discord since 2016, so obviously I’ve gotten used to the UI. The phone app was also largely the same as the desktop version until recently. For some reason, they decided to make huge changes to the UI. The first noticeable change is that when viewing a server, you can no longer swipe left to view the members and who is online. Now, you have to tap on the name of the server at the top of the screen to see the list of members. This is just annoying because I see literally no reason for this change to have been made. The second noticeable change is that the friends tab was replaced by a messages tab, so now you have  to go to your profile page, then scroll to see a tab you can tap on to see your friends. This tab also annoyingly displays your friends in alphabetical order regardless of if they’re on or not, instead of the original order of online and then offline friends. 

In essence, Discord made 2 large changes for no apparent reason, resulting in the mobile app no longer being the same layout as the desktop version. All this accomplishes is being an annoyance as it’s another case of a company changing something that functioned perfectly before hand.",1,208.1,gamestop to 5k,2
us,United States,10667951151,2023-12-07T12:24:55-07:00,Why move DMs?,"I like the midnight colors from this update, but please don’t move the dms. They’re fine in the upper left corner. The entire new layout gives me Amino vibes and I’m not sure I like it. It loads faster which is nice, but it’s difficult to navigate. I also miss the old icons… Also, my messages won’t stop leaving the text in the chat bar. They’ll send but leave duplicate text behind, which is getting very irritating to constantly delete. Please fix this. I still love discord, but please move the dms back :(

Updating review: the duplicate text seems to have cleared with refreshing the app, but it was too consistent to be an internet issue. I worry it’ll keep happening.

Also, after reviewing the user interface even more, I’m lowering my review from 3 stars to 2, since it’s completely unrecognizable. It feels like the sad child of Instagram and Amino, it doesn’t feel like discord as much. Please stop trying to adopt features of all other social medias. I find those apps far more toxic than discord ever was. I don’t want the same thing to happen to discord. I have a safe space on here, please don’t take it away.",3,207,ambrii_,1
us,United States,9737948559,2023-03-21T15:25:49-07:00,I love it but I hate it =<,"I LOVE DISCORD so much! But I have found one problem that makes me hate it. I know it is partly my failt, but it is also the devs fault. I used to have another account so me and my brother could do something for a game we loved, that was in July 2022. Then I got a new account because the other one was just for the one download for the game. My PC wouldn’t update Discord, and it wouldn’t let me enter the app before I got the new account.

     Then, when I got my new account I loved it! I met some friends and even made a collaboration with a developer of a mod list I was wanting! But, while I was meeting one of them in a collaboration, I went to get my email verification on the new account because I thought that you could use the same email on 2 accounts or that a phone number would work for verification. But when I did that, it said the email was used already, which it was, and it would let me get out of the verification process page. It hlitched and 164 messages have been missed! Please I beg you devs, fix it so you can get out of the verification page!",4,169.0,PeanutProGaming,0
us,United States,6056119245,2020-06-09T13:21:27-07:00,One very annoying thing.......,"Okay, so, I'm mostly writing this review to address a bug(?)that has made a couple things very difficult.
 
 So, I don't really know when it started, but for a while now, when I try to change my profile picture or set a server profile picture, it takes me to this weird place with the picture in the middle of a black void and the words: Hold and Zoom (I think, I have poor memory so that's probably not exactly what it says) And that's fine, except for the fact that when I press the button to set the picture as my profile, it zooms in very close on this *one* spot no matter what I do, completely excluding the rest of the picture.

 I'm not sure if it's a bug, but now, just to change my profile picture, I have to send the picture to my computer, download it from my email, and then set it as my picture, it's pretty annoying, especially since my computer isn't the best and takes a little while just to start up, and then I have to get to my email, which also takes a while to load.

I hope this doesn't seem entitled, but it would be very nice if this could be fixed or changed so that it would be easier to change a profile picture. (Especially for someone like me, because I'm constantly changing my picture)

Other than that, discord is a very easy to use app, and it lets me find people to make friends with very easily! I recommend it if you don't have a phone and would like to be able to chat with other people online.",5,25.0,Animalloving,1
us,United States,7503100000,2021-06-24T22:09:29-07:00,Idk,"I first got it, and I immediately fell in love with it, I became apart of a close knit server and worked my way up to a moderator, it was amazing until it didn’t. Things began to get toxic and lots of feelings were hurt. I can’t even begin to account for all of the times I’ve been cyber bullied on discord, it really sucked. I even started my own server but soon everyone in it began to hate me and tore it to shreds. All of my hours of hard work and dedication came to an end as I decided to delete my account because I could no longer handle the toxicity. 14 days passed, it’s finally gone, I’m finally free. So many bad memories correlate with the app and I know it’s the same for many other people. It’s not the apps fault, no, but it partly is for allowing bullying and harassment. It’s mostly the people who use discord’s fault yet it’s still correlated with the app. When I saw that discord was being advertised as judgement free I broke down because it was the most toxic app I’ve ever had and contained some of the most rudest and meanest and toxic people I have ever talked to. I would like to say more about my experience but I fear its 2 am and I need to sleep.",3,80.0,lexi1234567891011111,2
us,United States,10442897856,2023-10-05T14:55:58-07:00,Great to chat.,"Discord in my opinion, is one of the best chatting platforms I ever used, but, while it’s the best, they are some problems. Discord, listen, I understand you want to make the platform better by doing insane update, but it will be fun for some people who don’t have any money to have fun in some way, while using Discord. It’s really boring when your friend is always offline and you don’t have no one to play game on the voice chat game. I know that’s something crazy to ask because, YOU Discoed, might say, you can join server that some people made or join popular Discord server and talk with them, but that’s sometimes boring. I don’t know if it is only me, but Discord should start fun event, for people who don’t have money. I am not actually saying use all your money and give people that doesn’t have Discord premium, Discord premium, but something like a game Discord himself have made, or maybe, one section of Discord that teach people some stuff, like something new by just using Discord time to time.

I hope you understand what I meaning, but overall Discord is wonderful!",4,198.1,Report About The App,0
us,United States,13134901459,2025-09-13T20:16:05-07:00,very silly app,"ive made a lot of online friends on here!! before I was really skeptical about downloading this app because all of the …uh……. “interesting older people” …but, there are obvious things that will tell you if it is safe to talk to someone! most of the time they don’t have pfps, or descriptions/bios, and you can accept or reject dms depending on what they say! there are a lot of cool ppl ive talked to on here and there are a bunch of sunder duper cool servers and server tags to pick from and most of them have a channel called intros so you can put an intro, someone can dm you, and you can easily start talking!! there is a limit for the texts though, which can get annoying, and WHY is the nitro so much?? atp I just need someone to gift it to me 😭😭 but anyway, if u want an easy app to learn quickly and multiple of thousands of people to be online friends with, download this! I actually prefer it over the messages app then anything 🤕 but yeah top tier messaging app if it weren’t for it being known for freaky ahh old people 💔💔",5,296.0,jayyden :),0
us,United States,8229620988,2022-01-11T11:23:21-07:00,Its my favorite app.. but..,"Well, i love it and im basically on it 24/7. But i think the app’s age range should be down to 10. Why? Because kids dont care about age. If they are mature enough, then can get apps they want. Kids flood discord. And theres nothing wrong with it if they are mature enough. Age is a number and i know discord can have some servers that are a but explicit. But. The amount of kids knowing and learning stuff early is high and more kids are maturing too teenager level. Im thinking 10+ would be a great range for the app if children are responsible enough. Ive had this app for 3 or 4 years and i love it. I make so many friends. Younger and older! And there really isnt anything wrong with that. Kids need to be careful though. There could be kid settings too. Where they can only add people and join certain servers. So many kids use discord too. So it isnt a big deal. Coming from me, being 14, ive met people from ages 9 and up. I even found a lover. The app is great just lowering the age range would be a epic change!",5,106.0,K1raTheBest,0
us,United States,9701625253,2023-03-11T02:53:56-07:00,Discord app review only,"I’ve been using discord for years on my phone and always loved it. Recently, within the past three months or so, I noticed a bug where if I go to tap a person’s About Me section in their profile and they have links, the links do not work. Or discord does not register the taps to the links? On general posts, dms, and on PC it’s fine but on mobile this does not work. 

I contacted Discord support already and they helped me as much as they could but ultimately said they were already looking into this fix. This is a minor inconvenience to the app but I wish it would work normally as I use my mobile app quite a lot. I put four stars right now as this is the only bug that “bugs” me. There are other general issues with discord like if you’re scrolling in a channel for too long it will suddenly send you back to the beginning, or minor crashes once in a blue moon, but I don’t really have a problem with those. 

Overall the Discord app is one I use daily and one of my favorite apps. I hope that the link usage will get fixed soon.",4,168.1,Kiki Asakura,0
us,United States,7199424561,2021-04-08T12:39:54-07:00,Passwords are the worst,"Don't get me wrong, this is a great app. However, I highly doubt discord knows how to manage passwords. So I wanted to make a new account and use the same email address from my old account. So I try to do this, and I already know discord loves to shove verification down my throat. So I'm like ""ok this should be quick,"" and oh boy was I wrong. So I put in my email address and my password, but it gets declined. So I'm like  ""that's weird, I coulda sworn I typed it in right,"" so I try again. Doesn't work. So I try to use my yahoo account I've had for at least five years. Password is declined. I have never in my life had problems with my yahoo password so I just think ""ok let me just try my phone""
And I do that and try to put in my discord password (which I had next to me on some paper) and it was declined. Now I can't access discord. And if discord wants to respond to this, don't give me that ""Aw shinkledinks, it looks like a Springle has a rough day and doesn't have enough magic powder to snort"" that you are sadly infamous for. Like, at least allow me to view my password in letters or numbers at least. I would love an update where signing into discord isn't a multi-hour ordeal",3,65.0,BPBottoms,2
us,United States,6752180004,2020-12-14T04:32:31-07:00,Discord mobile has some issues,"I love discord, I use it everyday but since the recent update that changed the mobile layout it’s become very glitchy and made the app worse overall. PC discord is amazing and I rarely  have issues with it but mobile I have had 3 main problems.
