us,United States,6415422793,2020-09-10T10:55:09-07:00,A few bugs but overall it’s great!,"I love discord! It’s an awesome and funny app, and it’s great for quarantine (this review was made in 2020, where there was a pandemic, just an fyi if you are from the future lol) if you are really bored. I found a few bugs though, today I was getting more waifus for my harem (don’t judge pls XD) and the pictures showed up late. I shared that server with my sister, and she said it was doing it for her too. She went to go see if it was doing it for all of the servers, so we checked our owo testing server and the gifs showed up late too. We checked our server with our friends, dank memers memes showed late too. Another bug I found was that when me and my friend call, sometimes one of us can’t hear the other. Like, she asked me if I wanted to play a song with the Rhythm bot, and I kept saying yes to her, but she couldn’t hear it and kept asking me. Another time is actually while I was writing this review and she was talking to me and suddenly it was silent, and then I heard her again. Please try and fix these bugs! This is a great app though! If you read this, GET THIS APP!!!",4,38.0,~jigglyjello~,0
us,United States,6737716929,2020-12-10T06:13:04-07:00,Amazing chat service (On Updated Phones),"Discord works really well, and I don’t have many issues with it. The updates are interesting and keep things lively. Although sometimes things can be cluttered, issues are scarce.

That being said, glitches are more common if your phone or PC is an older generation. The phone I currently use is an I phone 8. Discord runs very well on it and I’ll only have a glitch about once a month or every other month. The glitches don’t affect the performance of the app, it just hides my battery percent, time, and cell service at the top of my phone. I am starting to think it is a system issue.

Overall, discord is an amazing app. My club uses it that we run at my high school. I have made so many friends and it is great for community based involvement. However, there are also a lot of pedos and groomers on the app too. If you are a minor and get the app, I suggest looking for other minors to talk with. Be smart, and don’t do anything sketchy.",5,51.0,ebvobevo,1
us,United States,14313853174,2026-07-17T04:17:02-07:00,Terrible report system,"There is a server with tons of defamation, racism, doxxing, threats and harassment that the in-app report system obviously doesn't catch. I tried calling but hey, that works as much as the report system works it seems. I guess I understand why the support system gets hated on, it's awful. I understand that some reports can't be reliable due to edits and inspect elements, but I even sent VIDEO proof in the email between me and Jean, and all I get is ""use the in-app report system."" Not even a, ""we will check through this and update you further."" This worries me about the safety of the community. People spend tons of money on nitro but discord can't even pay us back with a simple report review. Want positive reviews? Then review our reports! I don't like this half-assed Al era we're living in, because everything is just lazy. I just wish a human could actually read and understand the struggles OTHER humans are facing using this app.
Also, telling us to go to law enforcement is very inconsiderate. Law enforcement can't just delete everything, or ask discord to delete this server for being toxic. I've sent huge amounts of videos and screenshots, could be gigabytes of it. But no, I get this, as always.",1,337.0,Jinkeyss,0
us,United States,12675014753,2025-05-19T14:51:10-07:00,Discord is a traitor,"Discord partnered with DomoAi, an Ai image generator. Not only does generating an Ai image often steal art from real artists and then prompters get to claim that art as their “own” (imagine being an arhitect and after hours of building and perfecting, someone uses ai to copy your exact style but tailor it to their likings without having to build it themselves), but it also HARMS THE ENVIRONMENT! I can’t stress this ENOUGH! Generating an ai image is the equivalent of charging your phone. Do you know how much energy and resources that takes? IMPORTANT!!! DONT SKIP OVER THIS!!: if you dont remove this feature, then MAKE IT SO THAT YOU CAN TOGGLE IF YOU WANT PEOPLE TO BE ABLE TO USE THE FEATURE ON YOUR IMAGES/MESSAGES!! Just PLEASE make it a feature to not allow screenshotting/downloading/using this ai feature on your image. It’s so annoying that people invest in ai images instead of, for example, using ai for medical reasons! AI managed to detect cancer 5 years before it developed for a person, how about we invest in THAT and let AI do the BORING THINGS instead of the actual creative things. There’s always someone out there willing to draw ur ocs, like me, i don’t even charge money for drawings because, i spent hours on these drawings to bond with people.",1,279.0,Hyoasei,1
us,United States,10921236796,2024-02-09T15:22:13-07:00,New UI,"The new UI isn’t very good. It feels much slower to navigate, and I don’t like having a separate messages tab, because when everything was in one place before it felt much easier. My main problem is just that there isn’t an option to use the old UI anymore. In previous iterations of the new UI, this feature was available, so nobody was forced into it, and could keep using the old UI like before. Please add this back so that users such as myself can continue to use the old UI if they don’t like the new one.

I also feel like this UI change was unnecessary. There was nothing wrong with the old UI. Your site said that you wanted the mobile UI to feel optimized for mobile rather than a scaled down version of the desktop UI, but, for me at least, I use both versions, and them both having the same layout provides a consistency between the two that makes it easier to use. 

If you want to improve the UI, the best thing to do is to not change it at all, because “if it ain’t broke, don’t fix it.” Or just make the new UI optional so that those who like it can use it and those who don’t can keep using the old one and feel more comfortable with the app.",1,215.0,vhhfvhivdntvdhul,2
us,United States,10669051348,2023-12-07T20:40:09-07:00,New Layout Killed Functionality,"Discord has introduced a new UI layout that while very new, has a lot of features that kill the functionality of the site in comparison to the desktop versions. First, the new theme is harsher on the eyes for people who liked dark mode for accessibility versions. Second, it takes more clicks to get to certain pages, like finding activity and membership lists. Third, with the old UI you could automatically open on the conversation you were having, or if you got a direct message you could click on the profile bubble of your friend and be immediately taken to the conversation. Now it forcibly opens on the message page regardless of your last conversation, and now when you receive a DM you have to go to the messages page and open it. These may seem like small features, but make the layout feel more clunky and less optimized. Fourth, information is now hidden in places like pinned messages, where you can’t see images or previews of the messages which is what made the feature useful in the first place. 
I’m tempted to uninstall the app and find an alternative version to use. Don’t get discord until something changes.",1,207,Rachel lou,1
us,United States,8367985658,2022-02-17T21:40:45-07:00,"Love the App, what happened?","I’ve been using Discord since 2017, and I stand by it as the best public & private multi-platform media option around. However, at least in the past few weeks, I’ve noticed an extremely frustrating glitch that is only happening on my iOS devices, where the screen just doesn’t load the full channel I’m in, doesn’t let me type, and even more annoyingly the most recent change where it doesn’t send my message when I press Return on my iPad’s keyboard.

It sent my message after pressing Return for well over a year before now,  but now it’s requiring me to manually press the send button even while exclusively on the keyboard. It’s becoming incredibly frustrating, and because of how recent these issues have shown up, I can only assume they were unintentionally added in the last update or two.

I hope I’ll get a response, given just how positive my interactions with the Discord team have always been, and I hope the issues will be resolved quickly, but it’s immensely frustrating that this is such a new issue.",3,114.0,Vi$un,1
us,United States,5433138095,2020-01-21T18:59:12-07:00,Gripes about the User Interface update,"I have been a user of Discord for over a year and a half, with my experience being extremely positive. However, recently the user interface has been changed and I’ve received many complaints about it being too childish and distracting. On several occasions I have been accidentally voice called because of the UI update. I’ve also had a myriad of people say that is too cluttered and they preferred the older layout. My moderators struggle with all the extra bells and whistles strapped to the mobile version of this application. I am here today with a proposal for two different modes; one is for people who want to play with the revisions and the other is for those who don’t want to be constantly assaulted with a waterfall of bloat they don’t use. I know that I’m a single voice but I’m here to speak for everyone who’s told me their issues with the new UI. I just want my server members and friends to be happy and it makes it hard on them if they can’t even tell where the pinned comments are. 

With deepest sincerity, Elite Lunala.",4,3.1.9,Mangle Maniac,1
us,United States,10799155219,2024-01-08T08:20:50-07:00,Stop fixing problems that are not broken,"Discord is probably my most used messaging app. Before the new update it was great fairly simple and fast. Until now. This new update is so bad. Servers are in a separate tab which just does not make any sense. But that’s not even the dumb part. The worst part about this update is that when you swipe to the right it no longer shows the menu of everyone who is online (this applies to servers too). Why? It’s completely redundant because usually you hold down a message to reply to someone and it makes it hard to see who’s online or offline. This is an app you use to play online games so now you make it hard to see who’s online and offline. Just why!? I have no idea what you guys were thinking please go back to the original UI there was absolutely nothing wrong with it. Also when I updated the app the app size went from less than 700MB to almost 7GB!!! What the heck happened!!!  Please stop fixing problems that are not broken, you found something that works in the previous UI now stick with it! Please just give up with the new UI it’s complete nonsense garbage.",2,210.1,ReedJoel,1
us,United States,10461115602,2023-10-10T19:42:56-07:00,Payment is poor quality,"Ive been using discord for about two years and I've seen a lot of payment in it, in fact one of the newest features, app displays can cost $10 for each one, basically it is an animated gif that moves around your profile picture. So I decided to buy nitro, it is one feature that apparently makes your discord experience better. So I decided to buy it. But once i bought it, it didn't activate, nothing happened, and all in all i believe that the developers are just trying to wring a lot of money out of you. It makes you feel kind of wrong when you look at something like your profile and it shows “Animated profile picture” i think the system is okay but the payment for mobile just needs to be better. In the terms of service of the nitro it says that purchasing it is “flawless” in my own personal experience it still has some problems, but i do not think that they cant be fixed. So if someone is looking at this, i believe Discord is for everyone, but do not feel pressured to buy nitro. And thank you.",3,199.0,abram14283,1
us,United States,10359372418,2023-09-11T19:46:54-07:00,Doesn’t Connect or Work At All,"Update: The suggested troubleshooting steps didn’t work. However, I randomly tapped the tree-like “hub” button, and that caused a login screen to appear. I logged in, and now the app is working. I still don’t know why it stopped working in the first place or why it didn’t ask me to log in after reinstalling it until I tapped the “hub” button. I’m glad it’s working again now!

Overall, the app mostly works, with a few issues. It doesn’t play nicely with my virtual keyboard, for example. And if you accidentally don’t allow it to access more images on your device, the only way to try again is to restart the app. That might be Apple’s fault, but either way, it’s confusing. The interface for allowing the app to access files (so you can share them) is difficult to understand. Text chat works well most of the time.

Old review: Unfortunately this app doesn’t work at all on my iPad. It just says “Connecting…” but never connects. I uninstalled and reinstalled it, but the issue persists. I can’t even see my friend and server lists.",3,195,Blake598,0
us,United States,6541609865,2020-10-16T09:00:24-07:00,DISCORD IS AMAZING!,"I haven’t written a review in probably over 10 years, this app is so amazing on ALL platforms that felt the need to tell everyone who hasn’t used this app to PLEASE give it a try. It has so many amazing features and I don’t even know where to start. Firstly, you can use Discord to call another user as if it were just a normal phone call or FaceTime call and the quality is amazing with or without WiFi, it works just fine even if it is ran only on data. Secondly, you can turn a one way call, into a three-way call, four-way call, five-way call, six-way etc, this app is perfect for talking to multiple people at once. You can create long term dedicated chat rooms that can be used for multiple things, you can create a room, name it, organize it with labeled tabs, create multiple chat channels of multiple topics in the same room, unique tabs for sending images, work related topics, video game related topics, meme channels for only sending memes, you can create a welcome tab for new members to view upon entering the room via invitation, you can add rules to each channel to ensure they are used for the purpose which they were created, you can have a voice channel and text channels for general usage such as normal conversation, you can have a private voice channel for one on one conversation, you can even customize your profile with a chosen name and image. The name can be any name you want and there is no confusion between profiles with the same name since they are primarily identified through a unique 4-5 digit number at the end of each name. You can add a profile picture and bio as well. 

There is so much more I haven’t even mentioned that is just as important if not more but if I brought up everything I would be typing all day. 

Overall, Discord is an amazing app. If you haven’t tried it then you should. It’s completely safe and the TOS is very strict about safety and ensuring that you have privacy with your personal info and conversations.",5,43.0,Mist Star,0
us,United States,13741828965,2026-02-12T09:31:48-07:00,Deleting my account over data breech concerns,"I’m really disappointed in Discords decision to require government IDs or use of our biometric data if it’s unable to “passively verify” our age. I’ve gone down a few rabbit holes since learning about this decision, trying to convince myself to stay, and I’ve come to the conclusion that I’m not confident I can trust Discord’s ability or willingness to protect our data. We live in a world where a lot of  concerning things are being normalized: from our data being harvested for training AI models whose data centers ultimately draining our supply of available drinking water… to biometric theft and mass surveillance, just to name a few. While I appreciated learning that the 3rd party service being used for age verification wasn’t part of the recent data breach that leaked 10s of thousands of users data, I’m concerned about the probability of this happening again. I also find the notion of “passive verification” to be more than a little creepy. I understand that is likely the current state or trajectory of most big tech companies, I just had this naive idea that Discord would be going in a different direction. In light of all this, I will unfortunately be deleting my account.",1,315.0,Becoming Ungovernable,0
us,United States,12708584270,2025-05-28T10:32:36-07:00,Love the app but,"I use discord daily. As much as that's a cringe thing to say, yes I do! I also have more than one account, mainly for business reasons but also because the amount of servers I'm in can be ridiculous! I have a business, a personal and an exclusive pokemon one. However, when I am on the run I don't always have a pc with me. 

I would really love for the mobile app to have the ability to easily switch between accounts like the desktop and mobile browser have access to because the convenience would be so much easier than fighting the mobile web browser for either my pokemon account or my personal while logged into the mobile app under my business account. 

That implementation would be an absolute GAME CHANGER for this app. So many people use it and for so many reasons other than just personal. As much as I would like one account dedicated to it all, I simply don't have the patience to flip through dozens of servers when I can just have dedicated accounts for dedicated things",4,281.0,#TiktokTeaParty,0
us,United States,11743236931,2024-09-19T20:38:38-07:00,Good app with some bugs,"I’ve had discord for a while now and i can wholeheartedly say that this app is an amazing great app for calling, texting, and interacting with other people on the internet. However, that’s not to say the app is completely perfect. While in call, I’ve tried to screen share some videos or little clips to them and after a couple of seconds they would hear and see nothing from me and I wouldn’t hear or see anything from them, but my screen share on the top left corner of my screen would still show. I’d have to leave discord completely and reopen it to fix this bug. It’s been a couple of days, maybe even weeks, since it first started doing this. I do not believe at all it is a Wi-Fi or router issue due to the fact that it would only start doing this whenever I screen share or go to another app and it would simply crash. 

This isn’t a bad app at all, it just needs to keep working on bugs and other things so it can reach its full potential!",4,247.2,evannnnnlol,1
us,United States,10007083076,2023-06-06T18:53:04-07:00,dude how do i fix this,"heyy, so like ive been using discord for a long time, but i had an problem which i really hate. so like back then when i wanted to update discord, i deleted it and then downloaded it again, and like after it was updated i was texting my friends and i wanted to send a image, but then like it didnt sent. whenever i was on the website too trying to send a image too it kept saying “upload failed” and i really hate this. its not only images, i either cannot send videos or voice messages. and ive been having this problem for a while, like a month. and it really annoys me i didnt even changed anything in my account settings. i dont get how others dont have this problem, even though i keep redownloading it and i still have the same problem. so please if you can somehow fix this, please do it. plus whenever i go to discord, it wont load/open. it just shows a screen with the discord logo, like it doesnt load, so i have to use the website. so PLEASE fix this, i really hate it.",4,180.0,huvu KB cubcinn,0
