us,United States,11366475287,2024-06-10T12:57:53-07:00,Creeps!,"I really enjoy this app a lot, It helps me communicate with my friends and family sometimes. I always like to talk to random strangers on the internet and this really sparked my inner socialist, I enjoy talking to people on servers, maybe if we get closer we would move to dms! This is all so good. Until you get to the side of discord you never want to be on, the pedos and weirdos that try to get your personal information. I had deleted this app because someone had found my address by stalking my social media and by fooling my friends to think they were a friend from school. Although that’s creepy it’s still not as creepy as people who try to date me even though it’s online. There are also people who hate being themselves and always try to convince others that they are actually another person, it’s called catfishing. I honestly have no reason to hide anything other then my information, I just try to keep it ON discord and not into other apps like messenger. Unless it’s a game like Roblox or Minecraft or even valorant! I would still recommend getting this app.",3,233.0,gahahjanabha,0
us,United States,10667949019,2023-12-07T12:24:00-07:00,New Layout (12/23),"I’ve been an avid Discord fan for years. It’s been a great way to keep up with friends and look at cute cat photos. The new layout is inaccessible (for one thing, newly oversaturated dark mode backgrounds that make it hard to read the light text) and removes a lot of the many features that made Discord so beloved by users, such as having direct messages at the top left of the screen for easy access (which are now in another tab entirely, making it tedious to switch between servers and direct messages). The list goes on.

Discord staff claimed before the update that there would be an option for users to opt out of the new layouts, at least initially. They were untruthful when they said this; such an option has not been added. I know I’m not alone in feeling this way; every user I’ve spoken to (and many more outside my own communities and circles whom I’ve never met) has been upset with the new change and is frustrated with Discord for not listening to its user base. 

I hope developers take notice and do something about this issue, but I’m not super hopeful. It’s sad to see one of my favorite apps go this direction and I may start looking for alternatives :(",1,207,ReviewerPersonFella,1
us,United States,8858856121,2022-07-09T23:29:33-07:00,New Server Settings,"I love Discord so much. It’s my favorite way to connect with my friends from all around the country, let alone the world.

But I really wish there was easier access to change someone’s output volume in a quick, efficient way. Since the last major update/makeover of the app, it has become very annoying to do so. Accessing the list of VC participants requires clicking on the participants icon. Then when you are done changing one person’s output, it disappears and you’ll have to do the process over again to change another person’s. Long pressing on a person’s icon in the server chat is rather annoying. Accessing the list of participants used to be easier and simply required swiping up the tab. I am part of huge servers where there may be 50 people in a call at one time and I need to be able to adjust a person’s volume quickly if their output is too loud for me.

Please fix this in the next major update/makeover. Please… It was fine the way it was in the past. Thank you.",4,134.0,Lyssaroxx,0
us,United States,7498113374,2021-06-23T12:22:26-07:00,Tired of how reacting makes chat jump insanely,"This problem has persisted for years and no update has ever addressed it. I actually tried to go report this as a bug properly, but even that processes is so convoluted I said nevermind... Imagine a read only channel, where a mod posts an announcement that is too long to fit on screen at once. As you try to scroll up to read the channel, every time someone reacts to the message at the bottom, the chat jumps randomly all over the place. You simply have no control at all and cannot read anything because it jumps multiple times a second. Imagine in a server with hundreds of members how impossible this makes reading the post or channel (which is read only!) It doesn't just pull the viewer to the bottom of the chat where the reacts are either, it will repeatedly throw me back several pages and as I try to scroll to the message and it just keeps pushing me all over, wether my finger is placed down on the screen or not.

This is beyond embarrassing for discord at this point - if your basic features like reacts and scrolling cause bugs that make reading chat channels impossible, you have failed in your attempt at a chat app.",1,79.0,Sandy Amandie,2
us,United States,13737836988,2026-02-11T06:50:29-07:00,Fix Your Update Plan,"You cannot seriously expect people to submit their face or ID. OR let an AI spy on them. This is ridiculous. Our messages should be private, and no AI, or ANYONE for that reason, should have the right to look into them. This is an extreme invasion of privacy, and you will lose users by the thousands for this. I currently use discord, and have been for years. It’s a platform that I love. It’s a shame to watch it go to waste like this. My friends and I are currently looking for alternatives. You already have unencrypted texts, along with a safety function. I don’t understand why this is necessary in the slightest. Due to the recent development of AI, it tends to make a lot of mistakes. What if someone gets classified as a kid when they’re legally an adult for their texts? Are we then forced to show a picture of our face or our government ID? That not only confirms our age, but our very identity. There’s no need for this. You have no right to know exactly who each of us are, nor ANYTHING about our private lives. We use your platform for communication and entertainment. Nothing more. Stay out of our private lives, please, and thank you. Fix this, or you WILL lose your customer base.",1,315.0,Feyre._.Archeron,0
us,United States,10669501297,2023-12-08T00:23:26-07:00,Canceling my Nitro— New UI makes app annoying to Use,"Discord is my main social media that I use to keep in contact with my friends, but that may have to change in the near future if this new layout doesn’t get fixed. The theme colors are way too dark and make messages difficult to read with my astigmatism, and not being able to swipe left to see who’s online is extremely irritating. On top of that, you’re only given a preview of pinned messages, which makes navigating that aspect very confusing. 

Additionally, DMs no longer being at the top of the server bar is very disorienting, and overall the new layout is much more of a hassle to navigate. I understand that some people like it, and good for them, but I get so frustrated trying to use this app that I’m looking to find a new social media site to switch over to. What I don’t understand is why Discord has made it so that EVERYONE is forced to use this new layout instead of giving them the option to opt out. Until these things are fixed, I’m going to be canceling my Nitro subscription and encouraging my friends to do the same. It’s just not worth spending the money when the app is so unpleasant to use.",1,207,CJ MacPherson,5
us,United States,3948320080,2019-03-30T15:15:26-07:00,Great for going at your own pace,"On discord, a lot of potential stress about interacting with people is taken away since it’s mostly through text. (But there is also a verbal chat option if you prefer talking) If spending time with people in person wears you out or is stressful to you, discord is a great way to make friends at your own pace.

Edit: Since the new update, there have been in app notifications that block other things and can’t be turned off. In order to stop them, you have to mute everything which would also get rid of notifications out of the app which I do not want to turn off. These really takes away from the experience. I’ve seen developer responses on other reviews saying they are working on a way to disable the in app notifications and this will be in the next update. I really hope that update comes soon. Until then, I’m lowering my rating of a 5 out of 5 stars to a 4 out of 5 stars.

Edit: They have since fixed the problem.",5,2.5.0,Paraguas Pato,1
