in,India,4544146917,2019-07-30T20:12:37-07:00,Does not understand how iOS works,"1. Human enables 2FA on Discord
2. Human tries to login
3. Discord App navigates to I Am Not A Robot
4. Discord navigates to ask for 2FA
5. Human opens Google Auth to get 2FA token
6. Human reads 2FA goes back to Discord
7. Discord App has gone back to pre-login screen
8. Human goes to Step 2

Human weeps

Edit: To make it clear - the problem with this app is you need to switch to Google Authenticator app during the login flow to get the 2FA token. However when you switch to Google Authenticator and then come back to this app, it resets you back to the first step of the login flow instead of staying at the 2FA prompt and you have to restart the whole thing from scratch including the CAPTCHA. The only way to login with 2FA on this app is to read the 2FA token from Google Authenticator first and then start login OR have the 2FA app on another device and read the token from there. This is the only app which I have on iOS that does this.",1,3.0.8,jungleboi666,3
