gb,United Kingdom,5856262792,2020-04-24T00:22:09-07:00,Life changing,"Discord has changed my life.  Like many people it has thoroughly converted me and I suggest many other people join.  The big downside is that it’s not beginner friendly at all. You have to be very lucky to find a nice server at first or even work out where to locate servers.  Having used it for years though and being very familiar with it I think there is no better social media, no better communication tool.  I would definitely recommend it but only if you have the sort of personality which doesn’t give up, you’re the sort of person who can stand to research and find the right servers. Join hundreds before finding the right ones.  Once you get on a good server though it’s like coming home and finding a family, a community.  I think that’s what discord has more than any other social media.  A sense of community.  I would personally recommend Disboard as a way to search for servers, it’s where I advertise my server Hogwarts 2.0.  It may be less popular than Discord Me, but it is so much easier to set up, so you’ll find a lot fewer invalid links from people who haven’t configured the settings properly.  

All I would say is jump in and give it a go!  It’s daunting at first but so worth it.  I wish you luck and have fun. 

Ps.  Since this is a review of the app I should probably actually describe the experience. It is very smooth and well developed but could do with giving more pointers as to how to use it and there are lots of features you are locked out of on a phone compared to a computer.",5,18.0,elkinahole,0
gb,United Kingdom,11044109574,2024-03-14T10:29:50-07:00,Discord - pros and cons,"Discord is an app where you can join different communities and make new friends, or keep in contact with family/ friends. You can also make your own server and give out unique rolls to different members while you can create your own emoji’s and stickers. However, the downside of discord is that you have to pay for nitro which I think is really unfair because half of the prices go up to £100 just to boost a server and it’s unfair because not everyone can afford that money. I’d recommend toning down the prices a bit. I get it, we all need to make money at some point in our life’s, but you should think about setting responsible prices for an app and make Nitro cheaper…£100 for an app is just a bit much. I don’t think I would want to pay £100 for an app when I could be using that money to pay for a roof over my head. That much money is just as much how i would need to pay bills and it’s not fair on a lot of people. Not everyone has a rich life! The app does crash now and then but they fix it almost immediately, which is a good thing. They also have support which is another good thing because if you got bullied or harassed in servers/ chats, you can report the situation to Discord. You can also block any user if they make you uncomfortable. Overall, Discord is great. It’s a very chill place when you want to chill in your free time. The only downside of the app is the prices of Nitro and the boosts. In my opinion I think that customising your profile should be for free.",4,220.0,"Emily Roberts,age 20",0
gb,United Kingdom,11959184040,2024-11-16T21:42:22-07:00,The Continuation of these decisions will ruin Discord.,"I cannot begin to express how much I love, enjoy and appreciate discord, the app is amazing in every way, it’s useful and easy to access, a good way of being social and finding friends whether in general or on the gaming side of things, I’m in a community that I couldn’t be more thankful and grateful to be apart of. Here is the annoyance of discord, NITRO! Every business, every employee, every customer, every user understands the need for a subscription, it helps supports the business and makes it easier for everyone (in some cases) I do not kind the advertising of the subscription, what annoys me is that it limits features to the point where there’s no choice but to buy nitro, I don’t want to. The pricing is ridiculous. But I understand the point in doing it, the really frustrating part is that I can send ONE photo that’s the size of 10MB that is beyond ridiculous, there is no reason for it, I can’t send a good quality photo or video showing off my skills in the work of art unless it’s 10MB or less, by all means have a subscription, but don’t take away from the foundation that is discord. Charge people for profile customisation, boosting a server, but don’t lock key features behind a paywall, that’s just ridiculous.

Other than that, the app is flawless.",5,254.0,HerbalChief,4
gb,United Kingdom,5043193537,2019-10-28T15:02:49-07:00,"brilliant, been using for 3 years now","after using this for 3 years i felt like i had to give a review lol
brilliant app, so much easier and smoother than other social media that tries to accomplish the same thing. the way servers exist with channels for different topics as well as private messages and group chats makes this absolutely supreme for chatting with friends, and establishing communities. looks super smart, doesn’t take up space and is wayyy faster to load than skype or similar alternatives. brilliant for messaging through phone or pc, and looks/performs just as good either way. AND doesn’t take up much mobile data!! my only problem is with the battery consumption, but that’s the case with most social media- it’s probably more to do with the technical side of sending and receiving messages at such a rapid rate, but it would be nice all the same if it didn’t take down my battery quite as fast. overall, fab app, it’s amazing how the devs seem to just continue improving such an already incredible app :)",5,3.1.5,Rainbowkitty899,339
gb,United Kingdom,13601995226,2026-01-06T08:03:48-07:00,when im in a breaking an entire app to sell more nitro competition and my opponent is discord ios:,"Paying Nitro Basic customer, been using Discord for iOS on an iPhone 6S since 2018 You guys optimised it in 2019 and added caches moving in the right direction, then suddenly new UI changes and company direction post-pandemic and it’s only been getting worse since (I then switched to a 13 mini in 2021), even on an iPhone 17 which I use now. 
You took away native embeds, added pointless avatar customisation flashbangs and done little to optimise day-to-day use since. Uploads are outright broken or endlessly loop, the interface is gimmicky and dysfunctional and if it weren’t for the web client Discord would straight up be unusable. Even on Mac AND PC it’s gotten so bad I use Discord in a web browser. PLEASE PLEASE PLEASE fix the bugs, skim the bloat and as for 
slower connections and rising costs in hardware doesn’t keep up with the strain you put on devices when you add stuff no one asks for. If you’re gonna straight up rip off Telegram at least make the app as snappy and fluid. Back in 2019 I could connect to free NHS wifi with one bar and have a full conversation while waiting in a hospital. In 2025 even 5G isn’t enough… it all so tiresome.

Also screw orbs, you already take my money every month. You’re insulting everyone’s intelligence.",3,310.0,WatchOS enjoyer,0
gb,United Kingdom,3214268082,2018-09-21T09:40:34-07:00,Hmmm,"When the app works it’s great, you can customise your channel, add bots and do all sorts of things. Perfect for phones and tablets to be in voice communication with fellow gamers. It does have some serious bugs tho... if you log out and try logging in the next day you always get a message saying something along the lines of ‘this account was trying to be accessed from a new location” which to me doesn’t sound very good and would indicate that the program is constantly under attack by hackers. If you keep it logged in tho there doesn’t seem to have this issue. Another issue is that if there is a minor interruption in your WiFi it doesn’t reconnect but keeps you logged in, (people can hear you but you can’t hear anyone else)... also from time to time the server goes altogether allowing nobody online at all! This doesn’t seem to be very often but I feel that the issues regarding reconnecting after micro disconnects and the issues regarding having to stay logged in due to fear of your account being compromised is something to worry about. Who knows, by installing this app I could be being listened to even if I’m not even in a voice channel?... pls fix these issues soon. I’ve been using the app for months and have seen no attempt by the developers to correct what should be very simple errors and flaws.",3,2.3.7,NeonLitez,114
gb,United Kingdom,13711546533,2026-02-04T03:23:42-07:00,Great app but needs improving,"So the app is great for either school groups or gaming or music or anything else but I have noticed on other social media apps like Google or Instagram if you have 2 accounts, you can switch easily but on here even with 3 accounts you have to sign out  and log in again but it’s very annoying and I do not like it how it is, 2 I really wish we could permanently delete past conversations that included arguments as no one wants to remember the past arguments they’ve been involved in. Also you have to do something about bots and scammers. Also this app and company has too many places for drama and it’s becoming quite dead and making others isolated like myself like I feel like I’ve lost many friends on this app.

Please allow us to be able to delete DMs please and seriously please actually ban PixiePlayz25 she is ban evading and also allow us to simply switch accounts without logging out. And all the items are aimed at Nitro users, but I really hope you can allow us to delete DM messages so we don’t have to see the arguments or dramas from the past and seriously ban PixiePlayz25 since she’s been banned before and now able to use Discord, you need to ban her immediately for harassing me and manipulating me and other guys. So are you going to ban PixiePlayz25? She’s ban evading you know.",2,314.1,TheSquareTigerYT,0
gb,United Kingdom,7900249478,2021-10-10T13:05:18-07:00,It's a great app but...,"I really enjoy using discord! I've made many friends and overall has made me more sociable, although, recently my friend bought me nitro! I was very happy, the plan that he bought was the 1 month worth of nitro + 2 server boosts, almost a month later I told him that it would run out soon. Him being the kind person that he is, he bought me another months worth, but when I claimed the nitro, it went into my account credit. I emailed discord support and asked them about this, the solution is simple; just subscribe for another month's worth and it'll automatically use the nitro in your account credit, but the issue is, my phone doesn't have any credit card details that I can put in, of course, I could use mine. Since I'm only 15, my mother needs to know about my transactions, this is an issue because she doesn't allow me to have any online friends, and discord is literally where all my online friends are. Is there anything that you can do to change this feature and make it so you can just press ""Use account credit"" ??? 

Overall, I've had no problems with discord except this. I love the app and you should definitely get it!!!",4,94.0,Evelineee97777,27
gb,United Kingdom,10668040296,2023-12-07T13:03:11-07:00,"It was good, but they ruined it with the new UI","Discord in general is a brilliant app, I’ve used it for six or as years now, and always loved almost everything about it, up until now I would’ve rated it as five stars. I have never had any major issues with the app until now, they have majorly changed the mobile user interface and made almost everything less accessible, as well as removing the much loved colour scheme and changing it to a generic dark blue (this can be changed to completely white, or completely black in the settings, however if you want anything else you have to pay actual money for it). Before, the layout of the app was much the same as that on the computer but optimised for use on mobile through the use of swiping left or right to access things (intuitive and easy). The layouts are now quite different, and now in order to access the same things you must go through multiple menus.

Again, this application is brilliant for a variety of reasons, but I find it difficult to still say this as confidently with these new changes, the general opinion of which from the community has been somewhat overwhelmingly negative (my opinion included). 

Thanks for reading :)",3,207,Opathu,11
gb,United Kingdom,4687103314,2019-08-28T14:21:04-07:00,Go discord,I really enjoy using discord it is great but I wish they add co ownership this app is great for talking to friends making friends and a nice base tool for using roblox which can get hash tag out which can be annoying now it doesn’t which is great for minecraft and fortnite also many other games I enjoy discord as I have made lots of friends and most people are kind and it is in a controlled environment for younger users which I find safe and great having control but being allowed no hash tags is one of the nicest features of this app I have also found updates quite recent meaning the game is fresh and cleaned from bugs stopping your phone/iPad etc. As I use discord almost every day I feel this app is very good and I haven’t had any problems except when I was getting started the buttons can be a little confusing not that much though but after a while it’s just second nature the download for this app is really easy and it is a full on 5 starts for me I couldn’t fault this app,5,3.1.1,Harv2008,38
gb,United Kingdom,8434458110,2022-03-08T11:06:30-07:00,dangerous for children,"app claims to be 13+ yes? but allows nsfw & nsfw servers that can be exposed to young children easily, ive had dm advertisers advertise nsfw egirl servers to me since i first started using discord (2019) , and while i know you can change who can dm you and you can scan dms before they are sent, i dont think any person new to discord would know how to do that. they need to protect the minors on this app more because there are far too many servers that allow 13-16 year olds be in the same nsfw setting as fully grown adults, im not saying remove the nsfw completely because that would remove a big part of the audience, but there needs to be more rules around nsfw servers, such as ID before joining an 18+ server (that ive seen some do) - there is too much free space for cp to be passed around easily. im 14 and have had 15+ invites to nsfw servers (some that will welcome 13 year olds?!) in the past WEEK. I have turned off my dms since but it is annoying since i cannot message other people who are not on my friends list. It is unsafe for minors and discord either needs to add a whole lot more rules in place or they just need to make it an 18+ app.",3,117,lovelyyemily_xo,96
gb,United Kingdom,10018692174,2023-06-10T04:08:16-07:00,"Overall a great app, but..","Discord is a great app I can chat to my friends and everything haven’t encountered anything I haven’t wanted to, however there are some minor issues. 1 = calls- every time I’m on call with my friends it always seems to be lagging on both ends. I thought that it was just a problem with my device but it turns out it’s not. The voice seems to be cutting out a lot (rarely) the call abruptly ends and sharing my (and the person on the other end) screen is extremely difficult. The stream either ends randomly or it takes a long time to load and we have to keep re -trying. 2 = going into the app- whenever I click on the app to use it again it keeps loading and loading at first the problem wasn’t that big, however now it seems like it’s going on forever. However even with these issues I find discord an Amazing app to make new friends and keep in touch. (I hope this issue isn’t just with my device cause then this would sound a bit stupid, I do hope the discord team could solve this). Thanks for reading this.",3,181.0,urmum :),1
gb,United Kingdom,6796986178,2020-12-26T13:52:01-07:00,Amazing but a recent glitch,"So I’ve had discord for a couple of months and it’s been great so far, however the reason I’m writing this review is because I’ve recently changed the WiFi password to my WiFi and what happens is if I’m on discord for a long time it will start saying that the WiFi password is incorrect and neither is the old WiFi password. I know it has something to do with discord because I uninstalled discord for a couple of hours and all was fine, I installed it and the problem happened again after 20 minutes. As I said before tho it’s perfect apart from this recent error.
Update:
I tried installing it again and now it’s telling me to show I’m not a robot, and tells me to click verify once I’ve clicked all the pages that have a fire hydrant in them but what happens is that a second after I click the images of a fire hydrant it resets to a new picture and eventually I run out of fire hydrants to click on and I just pressed verify and it says that both my email and password was incorrect even though it’s correct and idk what to do. Please help",4,53.0,snsbab,10
gb,United Kingdom,6322982195,2020-08-15T09:49:14-07:00,Great app but have had problems recently,"Discord is a great app, simple to use and to make friends with and has helped me with my mental health during quarantine just by having social interaction with friends across the world. The app can sometimes lag during voice calls and when I have low battery but it wasn’t a bother

Last week Friday I was using the app normally when it crashed all of a sudden when I tried to open the app it was just stuck on the loading screen seemingly forever. I waited but nothing happened, I closed and reopened the app but nothing happened, I rebooted my phone but nothing happened and I turned my phone off for the night and when I tried to open it in the morning nothing happened

I tried again on Saturday by offloading the app’s data, restarting my phone and reinstalling the app several times and it worked and the app was functioning as normal. But this Monday, I was using it normally it crashed again and I had the same problem of the app being on the loading screen forever. I tried the technique which had worked for me last time throughout this week but nothing has happened. I’ve also tried installing and reinstalling the app and rebooting my phone as well but nothing has worked.

This seems like a very recent problem affecting iOS users and the fact I’ve haven’t been able to use the app since is upsetting and annoying because it is one of my favourite apps and has helped keep my mental health in check during quarantine. I’ve also had a friend of mine tweet to the official Discord account about my problem but we’ve gotten no response so I’m not really sure what to do next.",5,34.0,Daracoon911,0
gb,United Kingdom,10921113186,2024-02-09T14:27:48-07:00,Update,"I love this app and use it all the time. it’s my second most used app on a daily/weekly basis and to say i’m disappointed is an understatement. The ‘new’ update for mobile has ruined my experience completely. It’s made things slower to access and harder to access and makes searching things near impossible. it’s made the screen feel a lot more claustrophobic and harder to navigate. I managed to revert the update yet a month later Discord patched it and as i left my pc to go grab a screenshot from my alt account, i was hit with a jumpscare of the disgraceful update i had tried to get away from. There was no need for something that worked so well to be changed. The community has shown to hate the new UI and has been actively asking Discord to change it yet to not avail. It’s clear Discord themselves got bored of their app and don’t actually listen to, nor CARE for the millions of users on their platform. They would not be successful at all if it wasn’t for us Discord users yet they refuse to listen to us and instead constantly make the app more annoying and difficult for us to use. Shame.",2,215.0,FNAFLOVER123lol,0
gb,United Kingdom,9374868004,2022-12-08T11:44:55-07:00,Verification system?..😕,"Hear me out, This app is amazing for socialising with friends! I recommend this for gamers across the globe because it allows you to: Make calls, Stream your screen and chat whilst playing! I’ve got one problem though…Verification block?..I know it’s important to verify your account but to cut off all use of the app because you haven’t verified? Me and my friend share an email in a way, (She having created it for me to use because I was having trouble making an account in the first place), And that’s basically our only way of contact besides meetups, Which happen very rarely. I’m currently sitting on my bed, Confused, Frightened even because I don’t have her as a contact (We seriously CANNOT figure it out how to add others) And I really do not know when we’ll next meet. I’ve messaged her on roblox, but that hasn’t been replied to, It’s been 7 days, I’m starting to think she thinks that I’m ignoring her. Please fix this, Please do.

Sorry for the bunch of negatives, But I really dislike the verification system, So dearly sorry.",3,156.0,:3 😻😻😻😻😻,1
gb,United Kingdom,13655937727,2026-01-20T08:45:02-07:00,One glaring issue,"Discord is a good app. It’s a great place to meet new people, join communities and generally enjoy yourself. While you’re bound to find bad apples, generally moderation is effective at dealing with them (there are several instances where I know people who have been unfairly penalised by moderation but usually appeals and customer service can sort it out, moderation could be better though). It has its issues, but it’s functional and achieves what it’s set out to do. However, there is one glaring issue which stops me from giving it more than 1 star. In a recent update, every discord server now has 4 ‘hidden’ bot accounts that do not appear in the members list. They are bots that scrape a server for all of the messages and images sent and feeds them into an AI. This is all done without user consent and this update was added silently, so many people don’t even know about this. Frankly, this type of data stealing is disgusting and it may even be breaking some data protection laws, and I cannot give more than 1 star. If you currently use discord, then find out how to protect your data from these bots, and if you don’t use discord, keep it that way.",1,311.0,ThePuppet33r,0
gb,United Kingdom,7654899674,2021-08-04T10:19:54-07:00,Discord Review! (Used at for over 1 year),"Amazing app, I have been using discord for 1 and a half years now and it has been great. I’ve been able to meet new people and stay in contact with other people as well as find jobs that revolve around discord! It’s helped me a lot and was a life saver in lockdown. Discord has a discord nitro perk which you can pay for that truly does enhance your experience on discord so I suggest purchasing discord nitro for either £5 per month or £10 per month dependant on which discord nitro you would like however you can find out more about that on the app. One thing I would say needs to be improved is the upload limit for videos which truly has frustrated me however a perk of discord nitro is having a higher limit so you can upload large file sizes. Overall a great app with constant updates and fixes as well as easy help and support when needed!",5,85.0,Pizzakingsim,2
gb,United Kingdom,10676066430,2023-12-09T14:33:34-07:00,New mobile app layout is awful,"The new layout for the mobile version of Discord is ugly, unintuitive, buggy, unnecessary and an eyesore. Now, I understand that beauty is subjective, but when the majority of people (at least that I have spoken to) dislike the appearance of the app, you're clearly doing something wrong. The old layout was fine, and worked perfectly well. 

One of the ways in which this layout is worse is that it sends message notifications to channels you're currently in, which, especially in busier chats, can obscure text from previous messages with redundant information. I hope that this is a bug that will be fixed soon, as if it is a feature it is a horrible one that actively makes user experience worse. The way that you get to the member list or pinned messages in a channel is overly complicated in comparison to the previous version, which makes the experience of using the app far more difficult. I unfortunately have no way to explain this away as a bug. Yet another way in which this app is worse is that the in-app message notifications are in an ugly grey rather than matching the colours of the theme selected. Also, I have seen the prompt asking me to select a theme twice so far, which is rather annoying. The way to get to settings is confusing also, and as someone who enjoys being able to customise her experience in apps, the extra taps are unnecessarily cumbersome. 

Personally, I'd much rather at least have an option to get the old layout back so that I can feel familiar and comfortable with this app I use to communicate with friends. The only good thing to come of this is the swipe to reply feature, and even that came at a cost: losing the easy method to access members and pinned messages. Please either completely revert back to the original layout, or at the very least add an option to get it back locally.",1,207,Anq3liic,0
gb,United Kingdom,5987350130,2020-05-24T03:29:59-07:00,Voice chat issues.,"If you want to use discord I’d highly recommend the pc version. The mobile app has many faults that can make the experience frustrating. For example it never rings/notifies you whenever someone is calling or sends you a message even with notifications turned on. This can lead to people thinking you’re ignoring them but in reality the call just didn’t come up. On a few other occasions it has this strange glitch where it’ll ring like someone is calling you and when you answer it you find out that the call was a missed call from an hour ago and it’s only decided to tell you about it now. Talking of which calls randomly drop/cut off for no reason at all even with perfect internet connection so I find myself having to use other apps just to be able to voice chat for more than 3 minutes. I’m using a iPhone 11 with good internet so I don’t really understand these issues. Discord is a great app to communicate with and it offers some unique features, however I believe that they need to focus a little more on the mobile version because it can be frustrating to say the least.",2,22.0,bennickp98,15
gb,United Kingdom,11920985015,2024-11-06T17:32:53-07:00,Terrible Customer Service,"(4 Years on discord) The app overall is pretty decent. However, I purchased nitro a month ago and recently sold my laptop. I was trying to cancel my subscription but could not do so due to only being able to cancel the subscription on the device you paid for it on. So due to this I was charged an extra months subscription. I contacted the team asking for a refund and they cannot do a single thing due to a stupid “one time refund” policy meaning they only refund you once on an account. Which makes no sense because people hold their discord accounts for years upon years. I explained to them how I have recently been a victim to identity theft and my details have been passed to multiple different companies but they didn’t take it into account. Overall I find it pathetic it is so difficult to get a refund for an overpriced service which I didn’t even use or want and the fact it was such an effort to cancel is an issue in its self. The app is really good but the team is not. (I don’t often leave reviews if ever but this really annoyed me due to how long I have been using the app for).",1,253.0,Naieem247,1
gb,United Kingdom,10730515331,2023-12-22T03:00:15-07:00,Once was good but is now horrible,"The old version of the mobile app was fun and easy to navigate, but since they added a new Mobile update it has become unusable and is now putting a large majority of the userbase to not use discord due to its update. The lack of accessibility and support from this app is horrible, many people who have learning difficulties must relearn to use the app all over again and for people in general, nobody likes it. Discord seems to be completely ignorant of their users and not only tells people to delete their account if they don’t like the update but completely ignores the situation altogether. Additionally with the horrible new, unusable and unnecessary update they have added another update which deleted files/links within 24 hours which not only makes group projects harder but generally makes the whole application very user unfriendly. I would not recommend this app to new users, and would suggest to find another texting / chat app/ service that is easier to use. 

Oh, and you also have to literally pay an unnecessary amount of money just to use certain features.",1,209.0,Demonic_Dragons666,6
gb,United Kingdom,14140535618,2026-06-03T14:05:05-07:00,Discord watch your back,"I have done nothing but be kind, welcoming and funny. Never have I EVER bullied or harassed anyone. I am having a great day and then what happens you might ask? I look at my notifications and what do I see? An email from discord. Now, I am thinking “has my account been hacked?” BUT NO! My account gets restricted for no reason. I would appreciate if you could show me what I actually did wrong, but you have horrible developers who have no idea how make a friendly app. I am extremely irritated, disappointed, agitated, infuriated. Now I am assuming someone reported me or my messages, but knowing the world today you probably used AI to review my messages because you can get off your fat asses. The only thing I have done is joke around with my friends and yet you will let people send gore and other disgusting things into servers and dms. You guys have no real security and are just as bad as the isreal government. I hope you think about your actions and I hope your app gets taken over by the chinese government. I would say goodbye but you dont deserve anything good in life after how you have treated me and my friends.",1,331.0,OnItEveryday!,0
gb,United Kingdom,10931730142,2024-02-12T11:40:04-07:00,Layout change was a terrible idea,"I am not certain whether anyone in the discord UI team has heard the phrase “if it ain’t broke, don’t fix it”, but if not I strongly suggest someone introduce it to them posthaste. Their recent layout change has been an inconvenience since the day they introduced it and I sincerely hope they change it back, because it has notably worsened my and everyone else’s user experience. 

There are certain features that, since the update, just…don’t seem to exist anymore? You can’t search an entire server, only specific channels, and not any threads or forums (was the previous setup just too useful? why would you take this functionality away?) and to do so, the search function is so cursed I’ve pretty much had to accept that whatever I’m looking for cannot be found. Private messages and servers being split into two different sections is horrible, and makes switching from one to the other needlessly difficult (especially when trying to navigate with one hand). 

I just think bad choices were made, and I would very much like for them to be unmade, please and thank you.",1,215.0,193875929,0
gb,United Kingdom,1885027312,2017-10-30T01:50:57-07:00,Comedy is an effective tool.,"If you haven't been living in Skype for the past several years. You'll have heard of Discord. It's shares a few basic functions with Teamspeak, but is so much better visually, and in terms of its approach to dealing with issue. Take a read of any patch note and you'll understand. The developers feel 'human.' Instead of simply putting patches out there, ignoring the user base. They interact with them frequently, often requesting 'loading lines,' (Which, in this context, are comedic sentences that are displayed during loading screens). This comes together nicely, and has you appreciate the App so much better. Their  are bugs no and then, but the community will quickly inform the devs, and then they patch it. Overall, if you're a gamer on PC, get it. If you'd prefer to talk to people when console gaming, without the need of setting up mics and utilising the console, then get it. One of the easiest 5* I've ever given.",5,1.9.3,GaySynDis,52
gb,United Kingdom,7345642084,2021-05-16T04:19:24-07:00,"It’s great, apart from 2 things...","Discord is a great app to use! Contact all your friends to make your own private server, or join other servers with people that have similar interests! The calls are great feature, and you can even add fun little robots to do tedious tasks like managing the server, to bots with great dank memes. However, there are 2 extremely frustrating glitch which I know not just me have. And I’ve tried everything in my power to stop them from happening, but nothing works.

The first thing: the calls are great apart from this one bug. Out of nowhere, the other callers and any music playing from a bot will suddenly get very loud and really distorted to the point where I have to turn down the volume or take off my headphones all together; it’s completely unbearable. You just have to wait until it’s over, and it happens every 30 minutes or so. It’s very frustrating, as sometimes I can’t hear and/or understand my friends for a good few minutes waiting for the distortion to go away, and during the heat of competitive gameplay, this just simply won’t do. 

Second thing: after the most recent update, discord no longer gives me any notifications at all. I’ve tried everything, like I said already, to turn them on but they just won’t do it. It’s extremely frustrating and I would like to see this patched. 

If both of these glitches are patched, it will easily get the 5 stars. Both of these or not very hard things to fix, I imagine, I know you can fix them. But for now, you’ve gotta sort out your priorities, discord.",3,73.0,Free-2-play,0
gb,United Kingdom,9899402474,2023-05-06T10:42:10-07:00,The other users are ageist,"It’s a good place for Linkin Park updates etc.  the chat room is like being back at school.  If I mention I’m an older woman or state something from say the 1980 (hypothetically) I get ignored.  One user told me to use commas, again who uses a lot of punctuation in a chat room. You dare post something that should be in other chats it’s like you’ve put something obscene or rude, these kids weren’t even born when Linkin Park first arrived on the scene, and they judge me as I feel they don’t want to converse with me.  Sounds like I’m paranoid far from it, just thought it would be great to chat and share stuff with people who like the same music.  Nope it’s ridiculously childish and really don’t want to stay on it. Apart from my experience, the app is well monitored and has great links to other Linkin Park news, tweets, so it’s a good place but not if you middle aged it seems.",5,176.0,Loubennington,0
gb,United Kingdom,10210849925,2023-08-02T04:14:30-07:00,Really great! Except when it’s not?,"This is a little finicky because it’s not the app as a whole - the app as a whole is great! I love it, I use it all the time - it’s the number one favorite way I have to talk to my girlfriend (we pretty much live on discord VCs honestly)

However 
While fine for sitting in calls where there’s no streaming, it’s the streaming where it’s not so great now (in my opinion)

There’s the bright green bar of “watching _’s stream: [server name]/[VC name]” that NEVER GOES AWAY and is both very bright and distracting and makes you not really want to watch streams through the app, but also takes up a good portion of the screen when in landscape. This wouldn’t be a problem if it would not stay there as long as you’re watching the stream. 

The next issue I’ve had is as recent as the recent update and updating the app. Discord just doesn’t want to rotate. At all. Every other app will rotate, but it’s as though discord has locked itself in portrait and won’t move - as far as I can remember, my discord has always rotated when in calls, on the screen of that VC. And especially in streams. 

But other than those thing, discord is great! I’d just love to be able to rotate my screen to watch streams and do so without the obtrusive green bar being constantly in my face. 

It would also be kinda neat if we could go back to no call out timer in DM calls through mobile when alone in said call for 3 minutes. But that one’s more a “this is a minor inconvenience” than anything. It’s the green bar and the rotate that I’d say are my issues with using the app over PC.",4,188.0,Keyraina,0
gb,United Kingdom,12189027461,2025-01-15T15:18:07-07:00,Do not recommend,"Absolutely do not recommend discord anymore, i’ve had it for years on end and this constant need of updating had just made the app stupid and ridiculous to go onto? calls randomly hang up or it lags out so you can’t exit the call to text and have to restart the app, calls randomly cutting out and lagging saying you’re on the call when you’re not and not allowing you to join, the now mess up of the servers and chats is ridiculous as it used to be in one place and made things a lot easier now you have to click all different things to get onto a simple server. Along with how the updating has made it easier for hackers and scammers to access your private information and connections and try trick you into giving you access to your account or other connected accounts. Do not update discord anymore! this is getting out of hand the old discord was so much better literally i try calling people so many times and it doesn't even bother connecting me then the entire app shuts off",2,262.0,anonymous46018,0
gb,United Kingdom,11463092600,2024-07-06T09:24:39-07:00,you should read this,"okay so i don’t usually do reviews as most games are rubbish and aren’t worth my time, but this app, is amazing! yes it’s 17+ but it’s suitable for younger ages from 12 in my opinion Common Sense Media also recommends that Discord users be at least 13 due to its open chat. Because it's all user-generated, there's the potential for plenty of inappropriate content, like swearing and graphic language and images (though it's entirely possible to belong to a group that forbids these). now anyone can add you, but just close the dm, it’s good for trading apps, values, groups, codes and lost more! i recommend it for people who would love calling and texting there friends With its inclusive nature, Discord allows users to connect with others, find creative communities, network, and create a sense of community through feedback requests and support channels.",5,236.0,maisieIsSus,0
gb,United Kingdom,5787439891,2020-04-09T12:58:23-07:00,Great app! Needs some improvements.,"I’ve been using Discord every day now for 3 years and it’s great how it’s progressed from its earlier stages to the amazing thing it is now. There are some improvements that can be made.
For starters, I always get in VC’s (voice chats) with my friends in Group DM’s usually on my computer but whilst I’m in that VC, I’m also doing other things on my computer so when I’m looking through Discord whilst in the VC, I use my phone. But if I go into the Group DM to send a message, I sometimes accidentally press the join button at the bottom of the screen so then I disconnect from my computer and join on my mobile. The button is so close to where I need to press to bring up the chat bar. 
Secondly, I use Apple Pay to pay for my Nitro subscription and I can’t boost servers because it’s not supported with iOS purchases, which I don’t understand why it’s not, which then gets frustrating because one of the reasons I have nitro is to boost servers.",4,16.0,NoctoFrost,1
gb,United Kingdom,8393849862,2022-02-25T00:39:43-07:00,Ridiculously Poor,"1) very first time using this app, I had a very important group meeting - invite was sent with NO EXPIRATION & NO LIMITS. Several of us could no use the link stating “The invite link is invalid or has expired” 🙄 it was a brand new link and brand new invite. 2) I decided to start a new account, using it for only 1 particular server - And it seemed to go well for 12 about hours, I needed the app for some morning work. Then out of the blue I was removed from the server, i spoke directly to the admin and they said they haven’t removed or banned anyone. They send me a brand new link Lo and behold “The invite is invalid or has expired” so again I am unable to carry out any work!!! 3) I DM my friend from the same server on the App, yet again they send me a fresh invite, Lo and behold again “the user is banned from this guild”!!  I am questioning the developers on how poorly can you make an app? No person to talk to about any issues just a so called “support page” I have sent an email for the support team, and still waiting on a response!! My head feels like it’s going to explode with frustration!!",1,115.0,1986goat,1
gb,United Kingdom,5255583163,2019-12-10T04:00:40-07:00,Major Accessibility bug,"Been using discord both on desktop and iOS for almost 2 years now and honestly its fantastic. Ive made some great friends and incredible memories. However with the most recent update of the iOS app there seems to be an extremely odd bug when i try to load discord up while the iOS voice over function is active  the app tells me that discord has crashed, but when i load it without voice over it works fine. I need the voice over to use the app as i am blind. On that note, i would strongly recommend taking a look at the element mapping in the discord app and the elements labels. A lot of apps label their elements really obscure and it makes it very difficult to understand what certain buttons are on the app. Granted discord isnt anywhere near as bad as other apps but its worth knowing. Other then that the app is perfect and im glad to be a nitro user.",5,3.1.8,Devon Robb,1
gb,United Kingdom,8564335209,2022-04-13T16:32:38-07:00,Hate to love relationship.,"I’m not gonna lie, I didn’t really like it at first, it was just not for me for a while at the start- all those pingy sounds and the overly sleek background - I deleted it multiple times because of this and even after deletion could still hear the distant echoes of pings (hallucinations or a system fault, who knows?), like shrieks in the night - but I like to think that I’ve slowly moved into a state of silent admiration at the efficient notification system, the pings that give a rush of dopamine rather than dread and the very intricate details in the servers, etc. It is a sleek and efficient messenger. The only lag could be the one that causes as ‘could not load’ message to something you reply to that may be too far back into the past but other than that, it’s a decent app. 10/10 recommend to my bros and sisters out there.",5,122.0,Olive high school girl.,1
gb,United Kingdom,7432574755,2021-06-06T01:27:43-07:00,Misuse of Disabling Accounts,"Now don't get me wrong, I adore Discord. It's helped me form multiple online friendships and even contact my irl friends!! Overall, it's a pretty good app for communicating.

However, I am very angry at Discord. They disabled my friend's account for ""breaking TOS or community guidelines"". The email was very short, they didn't even tell him how long it was going to be disabled for or what he did. Discord has ruined his sleep schedule and his mental health. Discord was his everything and they banned him for no valid reason. 

When my friend got the first email, he emailed them back, asking what he did wrong. However, they replied with the same bloody excuse. After waiting 10-14 hours for another response, you COPY AND PASTE YOUR EMAIL. Your customer service is poor, we need real people to reply for us, not some bot who will copy and paste unreasonable excuses. Unfortunately, he isn't the only person whose account was wrongfully disabled. Many others on Twitter have reported their story. 

Please remember that this could happen to ANYONE, including you, so we need your help. We need to get Discord's attention so a real human being will contact us. On Twitter, please retweet the victims' tweets about their disabling situation and use the hashtag #DiscordEXPLAIN 

Your help would be heavily appreciated, I don't want anyone else getting their Discord account wrongfully disabled.

Sincerely,
                 stephy, a Discord user <3",3,77.0,stephy 😍,2
gb,United Kingdom,6407384546,2020-09-08T03:28:32-07:00,Better than other messaging apps,"First off I have to say. Discord is the only messaging app I use these days.  I am a gamer and I play with people from different parts of the country.  One is from Asia and one is from America and I am currently in Africa.  There is no lag at all between calls and it doesn’t take longer that 4 seconds to join a voice channel in a server.  It is just too smooth.   The use of bots in discord is what I say makes the app itself. You can program certain bots yourself or you can add ones people have already made into a server.  I play pubg myself and one time there were microphone issues going on in the game and we simply, without no hassle, we went into a discord call and it was in much better quality anyways.   I have been using this app for so long and I do recommend that you shall get it and try it yourself!      5 stars for me😆",5,37.0,preslarge,2
gb,United Kingdom,7769592141,2021-09-04T03:27:52-07:00,"Fun app, Dangerous for my kids?","I’ve been using discord for over two years now and I have found very few faults in texting and reviving texts. I love how you have added stages as a new thing and I also love how you can organise your chats into folders. (Although the folders can get a bit hectic sometimes!) I have also found a few things that don’t work as well.. Voice call sometimes lags out even when your both on three bars of WiFi. Video call, is no better as it freezes from time and time again. Adults. Kids are on this app a lot in the holidays, and are being targeted. One of the reasons I rate this app a three is because when a child reports an adult for bullying them or harassing them. It never gets dealt with. Why? Please deal with this issue as it is spreading very quickly….",5,89.0,Anonymas321,0
gb,United Kingdom,12115701543,2024-12-28T05:34:50-07:00,Great! But just one problem….,"I love discord so much. I’ve met so many wonderful people in the servers and I’ve been talking with them everyday on discord . We’ve even got emojis we can use in the server and they’re so much fun so use. Just one thing: I’m in a server with over 2.5K people now, but only about 20 people actually talk in the server and the rest usually mute it. Discord has now disabled mobile notifications. Now I’m unable to participate in conversations I would love because I don’t know when people are talking. I know that the notifications are automatically disabled after it reaches 2.5K, but isn’t it possible for those who do actually speak in the servers to have a button to enable notifications after 2.5K? We can’t really talk anymore since we don’t know when someone’s online so it would be really helpful. Please give feedback on this.",4,259.1,Maneet 325,0
gb,United Kingdom,14252525385,2026-07-01T23:22:19-07:00,great BUT,"I like discord and it’s probably my main source of communication… HOWEVER.. there’s two things that bug me. N1, the new appearance of the discord layout. The text, the messages and etc all look like boxes and it’s different and weird, and the text is weird too. This is probably just a pet peeve of mine, but loads of other people agree that I’ve seen, PLEASE make an option for the old one to be back! Begging you.

And the other one is the orbs. I use orbs because I can’t afford nitro or any decorations since I struggle with money a lot, but because I don’t have a computer I can’t do the ‘play __ for 15 minutes to win 700 orbs’ so I can only do the video ones, but there’s hardly any videos anymore and it takes so long just for one decoration 💔 it’s taken me about 3 months and I’m not even halfway there",4,335.0,Oliver n’ zip,0
gb,United Kingdom,7076291985,2021-03-07T07:43:10-07:00,Love it but always crashes,"I genuinely love Discord and I use it pretty much all the time. I love the emotes and Nitro (though it is a little expensive). When I’m on PC, there aren’t any problems and it works just great but when I’m on mobile it always crashes and takes forever to load. And there are also times where it completely crashes, logs me out and resets all my frequently used emotes. And it’s been doing that a lot. It gets really annoying sometimes. I have no idea why it’s doing that. It was working fine until a couple of months ago (I’ve been using Discord for almost 2 years I think). Maybe it’s because I’m in like 100 servers (was only in 20 servers until a few months ago) and my phone’s memory just can’t handle it. It might get fixed if I buy a new phone but this iPhone 8 of mine still has a few years left before it becomes unusable. Until then I guess I’ll just have to stick with Discord crashing all the time.",3,63.0,DXKing7,0
gb,United Kingdom,14397461081,2026-08-06T20:47:44-07:00,New ui update,"I have always been drawn to discord as my main form of communication as I find the features are supper accessible and easy to interact with. 

However, this new ui update is just ridiculous. I beg you to reconsider your decision with the ui as it genuinely makes a part of me feel disgusted. The fact that it looks like an unfinished underfunded website project is not something to be proud of and looks incredibly out of place. 

One of the main things giving me this impression is the fact you have changed everything to be in the shape of a rectangle or square with sharp, dull corners. It does not look cool, futuristic or appealing. It looks tacky, poorly designed and I haven’t met a single person yet personally who has actually enjoyed the look of this style. Furthermore I have had friends turn off their updates to PREVENT their phones to updating to the ui. 

A big thing part of the “rectangle” design is that in addition to the server icons, the chat box and profiles being rectangular the is the thing that stood out to me the most is the call ui. It looks so flat and one dimensional. Being fully honest with you it looks like I have grabbed the rectangle tool in PowerPoint and tried to recreate the previous ui but in quadrilateral form. 

Jokes aside, this is purely constructive criticism and an urge to you to please change it back to the old ui which was way more appealing and professional than this rectangular….. mess.

- nilly",1,340.0,Nillymilly,0
gb,United Kingdom,10731688076,2023-12-22T08:37:58-07:00,"Alright, but they make some pretty poor decisions","The platform works well, rarely experiencing outages, good latency times, very consistent. The problem is that they often try to revamp things that were perfectly fine as they were, seriously harming user experience.

Take the colour update they introduced in 2021. This was rolled out with no community feedback beforehand and ended up limiting how some users could even access the platform, as many reported the colours causing unnecessary eye strain/pain, with no way to alter it until weeks later when they introduced the saturation slider in accessibility. Too little too late.

The new UI released this year (2023) for their mobile app is another instance of this. The mobile UI worked fine for most users, but in a move which I fail to see the motivation for, they revamped it, broke muscle memory, and made no attempt to ease the change. Simply why?

Still, especially for a free to use platform, Discord is really good. I’d just really like to see them look before they leap into these big changes, as it always results in backlash for them. There are too many platforms running themselves into the ground to look like they’re doing something, and maybe Discord could demonstrate that it’s okay to not make sweeping changes as long as you’re in the green that year.",3,209.0,AyOhEe_AOE,0
gb,United Kingdom,5686769752,2020-03-20T05:11:16-07:00,Discord what happened?,"Ok so Uhm, I know something was really really weird at first when changing your profile, let's say I have a cat picture, it's either my profile pointing at the background or at its ears, this is a great chatting channel but seriously I do not want my profile to be a profile or pointing at its ear, Here's the story, I found a really cute cat picture, I wanted it to be my profile, but I kinda messed up, my profile was the ears, and if I try to zoom in, it still points to the ears or it's background, before this was really really normal, now what happened, does it have to do to you, Discord, or something went wrong in the picture, also I am using an iOS aswell, so I think that's the problem, or something went wrong, if you are reading this thank you, if you are up to help with this problem, thank you very much, I wanted to give you 5 stars, but please fix this problem, would appreciate if you've fixed this.",3,13.1,jrbarcena,5
