gb,United Kingdom,10671039967,2023-12-08T09:13:46-07:00,Just gets worse and worse,"Been a discord user since 2015, owned app since around 2016…

The past 2-3 years the app has gradually gone from very consistent and good, to poorer and poorer. More and more glitches would arrive yet nothing about the app would change.

Glitches include (aside from obvious unable to connect etc): problems with user statuses (showing offline when clearly not), problems with much older (and successful) messages appearing on chats and showing up as not delivered being in the way.. etc etc

Now they’ve finally launched a new update. Interface looks nice and practical.. will take getting used to… except they’ve ruined the whole app too. Not only have they COMPLETELY switched around the bottom buttons (which no one ever asked for) but I now get to use the app as if I’ve zoomed in with a telescope! And they’ve added message previews for every chat - which just isn’t right in discord.. I’d use WhatsApp or iMessage if I wanted that. The app feels much more overwhelming now.. 

You can’t see even near as many chats either, meaning more scrolling etc which is a huge pain if you’re in a group or 2 as well. 

Not sure if I enabled the ‘I am blind’ feature in settings however I’ve no clue why this fiasco is in place. 

I’d love to know: Why would the buttons ever be rearranged from how they were for almost 9 years? exact same buttons.. just ‘shuffled’ them as an April fools’ joke? 

Joke of a platform and continues to be.. making changes like this before even resolving the genuine headache that was previously present glitches",1,207,Icineses,0
gb,United Kingdom,10664406684,2023-12-06T11:46:38-07:00,How to ruin a good thing,"So a new UI introduction happened today (6th December) and so many very change changes have occurred on the mobile UI. 
The first questionable decision is the landing pad for you is your DMs and not your servers. While DMs are potentially the biggest usage for many people it’s nearly impossible to use discord without servers - so why shove servers behind this very large and ugly page of DMs and very large, low quality images of desktop icons for whatever the few friends that still have their “x is playing” enabled. 

The notifications tab is useful as it can be hard to see who and when you’ve been tagged and in what server. There was also no need to have an entire tab for your own profile, it has so little functionality that it feels like an attempt to pad out this new “tab” based UI, which clearly implies that it wasn’t a justifiable choice for changing the UI. 

And finally the colour of the new app, this very dark blue instead of grey for dark mode includes blue light, this is very disruptive for sleep and your overall sleeping pattern, the original grey/green was far better and should be reinstated regardless.

I’ve used discord for over 7 years now and I’ve found it so useful, but a lot of recent decisions have been baffling to me, I know all companies want to improve their usage rates and revenue - but let’s not ruin a good thing yeah?",2,207,Alexmgmdnckamxna,1
gb,United Kingdom,12311621862,2025-02-14T15:43:52-07:00,be careful people <3,"discord is a great place that holds great communities within, but once you join the wrong community by accident you get pulled into a rabbit hole of awful awful people. I’m talking cults, groomers and people doing overall illegal activities. These people will ruin your life if you don’t do as you say, I got off the app after i discovered this part of discord, so thankfully nothing  happened to me. I know close friends who have been victims to these malicious people. It’s not just discord this happens on but within these past years discord has been the worse for it. The app is known for its privacy and security, which is good, everyone wants that and it is no problem until people begin to take it as an advantage and use the app in wrong ways. If you have kids on this app, always check who they are talking to. If you use the app, be careful who you talk to. You never know what it’s like until you experience it. Be safe <3",2,266.0,Alrose72728,0
gb,United Kingdom,10668431628,2023-12-07T15:59:38-07:00,The issue with Discord.,"The new mobile app “update” has recently been introduced to Discord.

If you plan on downloading this app, please stop yourself now.

The controls feel clunky, many loved features have been completely stripped for the sake of replicating other messaging apps. (For example, swiping right no longer shows the members of a server. It replies to the message you swipe over. Just like Snapchat.)
In all honesty, it feels as if it has become less accessible.

The overall appearance is squished together and is extremely overwhelming. There is far too much going on. Image and video previews have been removed from the ‘pinned messages’ tab in favour of shoving as many messages onto your screen at once. 

Oh, but dare I mention the COLOURS! Even as a dark mode, Discord has somehow managed to make it TOO dark. How? I am unsure. The colours are so contrasting that it manages to hurt my eyes. The colours are TWO SHADES OF BLUE. Messing up this badly was unheard of until this downgrade was released.

One final thing.
Please, Discord, listen to your community. We do not enjoy this update, you have put every problem with it in the feedback option. You know we don’t enjoy this update.

You are not the only messaging app. We as people will not be afraid to move onto a new app that cares about providing a comfortable user experience if you refuse to be the ones to give that to us.

Unless you plan on giving me a response that isn’t automated, I don’t want one at all.

Goodbye. No “Thank you”, you do not deserve that.",1,207,Lauren_Draws,0
gb,United Kingdom,6799953931,2020-12-27T08:50:46-07:00,"Awful service, terrible treatment of users","This has been one of the worst social media apps I’ve ever used, been on the app for about 2 years and have had 3 different accounts, I’ve had them deleted over and over again for reasons that do not make sense as I followed every rule they had, too full of toxicity that needs to be fixed and full of weirdos and creeps, they are banning the wrong people, and DO NOT TRY to waste your time with them because they will ignore you for days on end or just give a copy and paste email, absolutely shocking service they need to get sorted out, good idea of a platform but they need to fix out priorities and ban the creeps and weirdos. Also when you ask for proof of the breaking of the rules they just send the same email again and ignore you after that, so in practice anyone could report anyone and get discord to ban them, or give lots of evidence to ban a certain person who has broken rules and they ignore and dismiss it, this app is shocking and discord i would advise to steer clear of",1,53.0,mase3452,3
gb,United Kingdom,5292782797,2019-12-19T13:12:20-07:00,Amazing!,"Great app! few bugs here and there, but they get sorted within the week.

However, one thing I would change is the support, rather than the staff members just copying and pasting a large text, Atleast have them actually look into the issue aswell, also it would be nice to be able to have a live support chat rather than having to constantly waiting for an email.

Also it would be nice to have the ability for server owners to allow stereo voice audio for us musicians on discord. What I mean is the Owner or any staff member of amy server cam check a box saying the person or role is allowed to use stereo audio, like what Bots have. Rather than us using a third party software like Ripcord. Trust me, if stereo audio was a thing in discord, no one would use a third party software.",5,3.1.9,BerserkTube(games&apps tester),4
gb,United Kingdom,6345967490,2020-08-21T12:02:00-07:00,Discord Review,"It’s a good, quick replacement if you want to chat with your buddies while you’re travelling or something, but having it instead of the PC version wouldn’t be advised.

- While it does notify you on your phone, it doesn’t make any kind of alert noise so I’m constantly late to reply to a lot of the messages I get @‘d in, having this feature would improve greatly for more on-the-go people who have to commute daily and etc.

- There’s quite a bit of difficulty in joining new servers through bots. This might just be due to the Iphone’s app store or whatever, or because of something the bot’s doing wrong, but I always end up getting re-routed to the app store and that interferes with the joining server process, so you can only really join new servers through being invited personally or having an actual link to the discord being dm’ed to you by someone else.

- Making servers and managing them, either as a server owner or a server administrator/moderator is very tedious compared to the PC version, It’d be nice if this was improved upon so certain phone features would be improved so it is easier to navigate the server settings and etc. For example the nickname change option is hidden under 3-4 menus and sub menus, when It could be just holding onto your status changer in the bottom left corner and then pressing change nickname through that or something.

Overall, discord is still my no.1 app for socialising online but I would recommend getting another version of discord along with it, and using this one as a temporary replacement if you want to chat to your buddies without access to a PC or one of the other platforms that you can run discord on.",3,35.1,Osphin,0
gb,United Kingdom,13733918449,2026-02-10T04:54:24-07:00,March update,"Global age verification as of next month, otherwise your account is treated automatically as if you’re 13 years old. Even if you have held the account for over 10 years. With the recent introduction of age verification for discord within the UK last year, it took all of two months for thousands of people’s information to be hacked. 
All under the guise of protecting children, though surely this would just make it easier for those bad characters to identify exactly who they are targeting on the platform now. 
DO NOT trust this platform to hold your sensitive information. Once it goes to their third party holders, they cannot issue a guarantee that your info is actually deleted. 

On top of this, they will also be introducing an AI bot that scans every message you send, and if that bot deems you to be underage, even AFTER verification, you will be flagged and once again need to verify. Very stupid direction for this once beloved platform to be going.",1,315.0,~~Sin~~,1
gb,United Kingdom,13679706974,2026-01-26T16:57:59-07:00,Falsely accused,"On 26 Jan 2026 I have received a message from discord that I broke the community guideline during work so I didn't really think much of it because I was at work. When I'm home I called and when I wanted to screenshot for my Minecraft stuff, I was not able to and that's when I got curious to why I can't as I haven't done anything. 

