gb,United Kingdom,10668012511,2023-12-07T12:51:01-07:00,Good app destroyed by a really dumb layout change,"What’s with the new layout? I get if discord was improving the app for the better, by for example listening the what the user-base wants, but going around and completely ruining the discord layout in order to literally copy the layout of other apps.

The layout on the app itself has been changed so badly that it’s essentially nothing like discord on desktop, making it a nightmare to switch between both, and the common task of seeing what friends are active and offline has been made harder by having to open a completely new menu, as discord wants to further promote a feature that people *kinda* use but usually don’t need to most times (replying to other messages)

Moving DMs and Group DMs into its own category at the bottom is often confusing at times and is completely pointless, especially to us who use discord as a place to have group DMs as we don’t want to deal with the hassle of creating a whole group discord server, which often causes WAY more drama than a quick and simple group DM.

Overall I think discord should reconsider this update or *at least* have an option to revert back to classic discord. So far the response from discord has quite literally been to tell people to leave the platform instead of providing an option to revert.",1,207,Nowsk125,0
gb,United Kingdom,7081146998,2021-03-08T15:13:08-07:00,Awful platform,"This is not so much about the app , but discord in general, it's about as complicated and as user unfriendly as a platform can get.. I work in IT and I can't fathom it out... Login is hidden, you get silly messages telling you to claim an account, then says the account aleady exists... Yes it does so why not just let me bloody login then instead to claim my account .. geeze .. trying to join a channel should not be this hard... I don't want to install the app, I've got discord in my browser , but when trying to join a new channel, why oh why are you forcing me to download the app.. to join ??? Seriously I've never ever come across an app so complicated ..  arrrrrrrrghhhhhh!!!",5,63.0,PaulBrUk2010,0
gb,United Kingdom,4134630194,2019-05-11T09:46:47-07:00,Best app but..,"I really like the app but it is missing a lot of features from the desktop version. One of the feature i would love to see is the ability to actually jump to a chat from search bar. I don’t know why the search bar is there if it doesn't jump to the actual message that you can edit/delete/react to. Also the ability to mark a channel or the whole server as read so you don’t have to go through every channel to remove those white unread dots. These small things will really make the mobile version a lot better. And ability to jump to pinned message and being able to edit. Lastly, if we get a little tweaked version of discord for iPad which looks alot more like desktop version, i think that would be a game changer. Thanks!",4,3.0.1,Asadkhan101,1
gb,United Kingdom,10667777122,2023-12-07T11:14:48-07:00,I’m so sick of this stupid app,"It’s was actually good. A nice sleek design different to all other apps I’ve come across. I find it hard when theres too much on the screen so the way you could just swipe made it really enjoyable and accessible. There was a slight learning curve getting used to everything but I’d say it was definitely one of my favourite apps for the interface.

Though for whatever reason the people in charge are deadset on ruining the experience for everyone. The new interface no one wanted and no one likes. It’s clunky, stressful and hectic. You can’t see who’s online anymore making navigating servers exceedingly difficult. It was my go to place for group chats surrounding uni work and basically everything but this new update has put me off. I hope the creators can actually listen to their audience and fix it or I’ll have to find a new platform as I’m sure many others will too.",1,207,connor0273827832792,0
gb,United Kingdom,10669929821,2023-12-08T03:26:51-07:00,New UI update broken features and headaches,"The new ui update has removed the ability to see who is online in a server.  This is disastrous for trying to do work or school projects. It also makes it essential impossible to moderate your server from a mobile device so large servers are effectively unmoderated hell scapes of spam and phishing attacks until a mod walks back to a desktop. 

They’ve made the replies hidden behind two taps instead of one and made the design less ergonomic, discord can no longer be used one handed as a disabled user this most recent update is extremely frustrating as one of the most accessible comms apps I no longer can use without putting my phone down on a surface. 

The hiding of dm makes it harder to respond to them instantly which is forcing our project to relay on email again as you can’t see dm without going to the messages tab. 

Pinned messages no longer show any embed so art or cinema servers or meme servers are now broken. This also makes it impossible to see context as the full text of a pinned message or notification is no longer being displayed. 

I’ve also been told by a friend the new dark mode is so high contrast that it gives them headaches. 

We are seriously considering cancelling our multiple nitro subs and moving our whole team to slack.",1,207,J J E Hinchliff,0
gb,United Kingdom,10664990531,2023-12-06T16:08:17-07:00,I love discord but I can’t use this until it’s fixed,"I love using discord it a brilliant way to connect with friends and work on projects but I can no long use the app after its newest update. I suffer from dyslexia and the old dark mode was perfect as I could read all the text. Unfortunately now text and void merge into one and I can no longer read. Midnight mode is far worse looking like darkness with white glare and light mode just hurts my eyes. I tried to use the feedback site but it didn’t work so I’m putting light on the issue here, I do hope the dark mode could be added back or returned to how it was as I would like to be able to read my messages without waiting to return home and open my computer.",4,207,RaylaTheStormSpirit,0
gb,United Kingdom,6027416860,2020-06-02T14:58:31-07:00,Really good app! Could use some improvements,"Discord is a really fun and friendly app! In my experience, Everyone respected my choice of speaking or not :) Everyone was fun and friendly and I couldn’t be happier! I’ve made some amazing friends that I hope will continue for a long time to come! At first I was really nervous about is this appropriate for my age? Will they discuss things that concern me? But everyone was friendly and understanding and aware the use of inappropriate language would not be tolerated. If you were concerned about your child using this app I would recommend your child should be above age 10 and trust they will be responsible online. The only thing is sometimes discord has some connection issues causing glitching and audio issues. 
