gb,United Kingdom,10668269092,2023-12-07T14:45:33-07:00,The new UI is an accessibility nightmare.,"Only within the last few days as of writing this, Discord has rolled out a new UI, and it’s awful. 
I’ve been a daily Discord user for almost 4 years now, and the old UI was perfect for me! I have never had an issue with it. Neither had most users. However this new UI has been forced upon every user (whether they had auto updates on or not), with no option to revert back. 
Three things stand out:
1. The new colour options. All of them are bad. Light mode is too bright, and for many people such as those prone to migraines are unable to use it. Dark mode is too dark (as opposed to the previous grey colour) and the contrast is higher, so many people with a variety of visual problems are finding the app hard to look at or even physically painful to use. Midnight mode is just a worse dark mode. 
2. The new layout. Everything has been split into unnecessary tabs. Whilst the server tab remains mostly the same, the main search function and member list view are now compacted into one place and more awkward to access and use. DMs have changed entirely, and settings has more tabs than necessary. This is inaccessible for so many, especially those who rely on routine or have cognitive disabilities. 
3. In general, the app is now more prone to lag and slowness, both due to the new layout being unnecessarily complicated and general app performance. 
Overall, a perfectly good messaging app has been ruined in favour for a needlessly confusing UI, making it more inaccessible without fixing the already existing accessibility problems (e.g. not enough contrast/colour settings). 
Discord need to get their game on to focus on the real app problems instead of forcing users into an unwanted app design just to fit in with the competition. It’s disgraceful.",1,207,Chauffeured random,0
