gb,United Kingdom,12132644045,2025-01-01T11:30:11-07:00,No obvious documentation on supported video formats makes video sharing difficult.,"When trying to share videos, it becomes clear that many video formats don’t work in Discord’s app. For example, webms seem to play fine in Discord in the browser, even on mobile, but they won’t play in this app.

It wouldn’t be as much of an issue if Discord had a page on what video formats work on which devices, yet there is no clear information on what formats can be used. Discord has a video codecs faq page that seems to suggest that AV1 is supported, but last time I tried to upload an AV1 mp4, it didn’t work. The only way to test if a video will work seems to be to actually try posting it!

MP4s with h264 seem to be the only safe option right now, but these video files easily get too big.

