ca,Canada,10745840864,2023-12-25T23:10:39-07:00,I love discord BUT,"I love using discord, it is one of the only social platforms I use! But with the new update to the app, they made it so much worse. In this review I will detail what I mean specifically.

1: they moved the dm section from the top of the server list to a bar at the bottom of the screen. This makes it incongruous with the desktop version. 

1.5: More on the incongruity between the app the the desktop version. With the moving of the dms, the lack of perceived placement of the ‘who’s online list’ the app becomes harder to figure out if you mainly use desktop. When I first used the app version of discord, it was very intuitive because it was like the desktop version. Making them mismatch breeds confusion when trying to learn the app.

2: They have made it so that swiping to the left makes you enter reply on whatever message you had your finger on, instead of taking you to a list of who is online.

3: This may not be the case for everyone but I also experience noticeable stuttering whenever I try to switch between my list of servers, and the chat I’m in, or do anything really.

4: they made dark mode darker, which made the contrast between the words and the background worse, it makes my eyes hurt and borders on giving me a headache.

5: More minor dislikes. I do not like the new headphones icon, headphones like that would never sit comfortably on your head. 

5.1: I may be off my rocker for this one, but, I find that most of the new icons just look unfriendly, and harsh. 

5.2: There wasn’t a need to change the server sections icon to a group of houses, that is the section for what discord as a platform is known for, it made sense to have the logo there.",1,209.0,DisorderlyConduct,3
