ca,Canada,10752102966,2023-12-27T12:25:48-07:00,Disappointing Discord Update – A Struggle for Autistic Users,"As an individual with autism, I find Discord's new UI update to be deeply challenging. The relocation of swipe features has created an unnecessary hurdle, disrupting the intuitive flow that many of us rely on for comfort and efficiency. The visual overhaul is not only jarring but fails to consider the needs of neurodivergent users who often thrive on familiarity. What's particularly disheartening is the absence of an option to revert to the old appearance. The sudden, major change feels overwhelming and unsettling, neglecting the diverse user base that Discord serves. Autistic individuals, like myself, often find solace in routine and familiarity, and this update has regrettably disrupted that equilibrium. Discord's decision to implement such a drastic change without adequate consideration for neurodivergent users reflects a lack of empathy and understanding. This update not only misses the mark on user experience but also leaves a significant portion of its community feeling disregarded and disconnected. One star for a UI update that not only misses the mark but actively infringes on the comfort and accessibility of autistic individuals.",1,209.0,MintedMike,2
ca,Canada,10736114587,2023-12-23T10:14:30-07:00,Newest mobile update…,"used this app for years, big fan overall especially of the computer version of it. however, the newest mobile update is ATROCIOUS. irredeemably terrible, and barely functional. it’s impossible to see when you get a DM because that tab is so low contrast and weird, the server notification icon on the bottom is really annoying with its constant blue dot. overall, they added absolutely nothing useful and made gratuitous annoying changes for no reason. 

look discord, at least let me opt out of this awful new mobile layout. my friends and I hate it so much we did a gaming call over INSTAGRAM, which is insane.",1,209.0,PlatyGirl 1O1,2
ca,Canada,10730039867,2023-12-21T23:54:40-07:00,Oppressive Design,"As of the recent update (AppleVer.209.0), Discord Mobile has been reduced to a sad, generic social media platform. 

Discord used to be simple, the Servers and Direct Messages were easy to navigate; You could look at a orderly list of your online friends and their current activity; The Profile Editor was simple but effective. 
The Old Discord Mobile was perfectly fine the way it was. 

The new Discord Mobile? 

The Discord Team has gutted the clean app design and replaced it all with an unintuitive mess of bubble buttons and cluttered “organization”. 

The current Discord Mobile is akin to a Social Media Platform, with “adjusted” categories and changed inputs, this app feels more like a mix between Instagram and Snapchat. 

Here is a breakdown of the actual problems that the new UI has:

“Swipe to Reply” causes many issues as it makes app navigation more difficult. The whole purpose of “Swipe to Reply” is to make it easier for people to use one hand while texting. There is no reason to use only one hand while on Discord. This also conflicts with the next point. 

The app is now organized into 4 categories of “Servers”, “Messages”, “Notifications”, and “You”. The old UI had servers and Messages in the same section. This was convenient as it condensed the two categories into one, and it was set up in a relatively easy to navigate manner. While it is arguably easier to navigate the app now compared to before thanks to this separation, you have to ask why they were separated. It is now easier to open the server tab on the new UI when using only one hand. Thats fine and all until you look at the server tab. It is organized in the exact same way as it used to be, servers on the left side, starting from the top of the screen down to the bottom. This is contradictory to the main argument of using the new UI, as it is equally as difficult to navigate the servers tab with one hand now as it was in the previous UI. 

There are also “features” that aren’t clear, double tapping the “You” page to quickly go to settings, but adding no other double tap features for the other tabs? 

All of these statements have been ignoring my preference for the way the app *Looks* and has focused on how it *Feels* and how it *Works*. This app Feels and Works like a mix of Instagram and Snapchat, yes, but it Looks much, much worse than both of those apps. 

The design also has flaws. Everything feels round and clunky. I want to see what my friends are up to? I have to open their DM, and click on their profile. Why am I going to their DM instead of clicking on their profile at the top of the page? Because the top of the page has both missing entries and no organization to its order. How am I supposed to find my friend’s status in the top row when it is that unreliable. 

Everything is overly large and unexplained. It made a ugly pallet change from the dark grey to a navy/dark blue, and the Midnight theme is not a good alternative. Everything is now swipe swipe swipe. This is just sad. You took a good thing and destroyed it. 

And worst of all? Discord has decided to not let users revert to the old UI. It has been stated in their update FAQ, and it is depressing that they are restricting its users like this. Especially for those on the Apple platform, not being able to re-install an older version of the app with an APK file. 

TLDR: New Discord UI bad. Old Discord UI good. Bring back Old UI. Throw out the New UI.",1,209.0,User4756,2
