au,Australia,9624836121,2023-02-16T15:46:16-07:00,Excellent app!,"This app is amazing! It’s really good for talking to friends, and I like the idea of making your own server, however, I want something to be added. Can there be a feature where you can see history of old friends, and make it so you can add them back? Also if you have their discord name or old discord name, can you make it a feature so that you can see everyone with that existing name, or current name, and be able to add them? Overall though apart from adding old friends (which is fine) I would highly recommend this app. To all the parents, the 17+ rating is pretty over exaggerated, as you can block someone or unfriend them, whenever you like. The only problem is that if you have not many privacy settings, you could see some explicit content, however like I said before, you can block and unfriend then whenever you like. Would recommend.",5,165.0,Huper games,1
au,Australia,10944351539,2024-02-16T01:28:57-07:00,Was my number 1 messaging app on mobile,"Discord has been an app I used for a long time, it was an incredible app that was easy on the eyes and even easier to use. Then they changed the ui and gave NO way to switch back. I have seen people’s comments on this new ui talking about how buggy it was but that wasn’t my main issue. The issue I had was all my muscle memory is no longer applicable thanks to the changes. Luckily a YouTuber posted a way to revert to the old ui using console. HOORAY… a month later they patched it and within 30 seconds (not an exaggeration) of opening the app all the buttons froze and I had to restart discord. Some people with medical issues also have been negatively affected. While I haven’t used the new layout a lot, I speak for a lot of people when I say it’s garbage The only reason that I don’t give one star is because the pc app didn’t get a new ui. Worst app update I’ve ever seen in my entire life and I will be downgrading discord to before the ui update despite any security issues that don’t get patched with the old versions.",2,216.0,Omnex_,1
au,Australia,11492437553,2024-07-14T08:06:37-07:00,I love it POOKIES🤘🤘🤘,This is not a bot btw I love discord because I can talk to my friends and join and make servers with my friends or YouTubers or anyone really I can also join study groups and clubs so you can use it for your own personal use or your school work. I would Definitely recommend this app for young adults or teens because it might or can be an unsafe platform for young kids but I have not seen anything unsafe or something like that. If you do let a young kid on here please make sure to supervise them and protect them from anything that can come up because just remember it’s an online app! So in my opinion I would recommend discord to 12+ people and I know it says that it is a 17+ app but my 12 and 15 kids have it and they seem to love it and like I said before I have not seen anything bad or unsafe I just putting it out there that it might and can occur. I hope this helps 👍⭐️,5,237.0,#The lover of Roblox,1
au,Australia,3253695608,2018-10-01T19:08:33-07:00,It’s a cool app,"What can I say... the app is great and looks cool 😎, the bugs get fixed (probably by fixing them, good job coding peeps) the improvements to the app make it better and that’s not a given, and the update logs are a source of puns and funny comments. The app is great to be apart of a community, have a group chat with friends (over some games) or to talk with distant relatives because teleportation isn’t available yet in this patch of Life. Now if only light theme could disappear, that would be great. I recommend gradually changing the white theme to dark theme, going through a few shades of grey (more than fifty tho) they won’t notice a thing if the transition is done smoothly :^) 
But yeah, discord is a solid 5/5, the Discord team did (and is still doing) a great job with this app. Buy it (for free) to be cool today (I mean you can also pay to be extra cool but you don’t have to (you’d be extra cool tho, which is cool))",5,2.3.8,Jojofoulk,49
au,Australia,10677915286,2023-12-10T03:01:29-07:00,UI change has brought this app from 4 stars to 1,"The new UI is absolutely atrocious. Numerous users have been complaining about accessibility issues (such as the decision to alter the dark mode to make it *less* accessible to users with astigmatism), poor design, moving essential app features previously accessible through a single swipe or tap to behind multiple swipes, taps and button presses seemingly moved to completely obscure locations. Additionally, the new UI features a number of (potentially dangerous) bugs, ranging from infinite loading screens to crashing when certain inputs are made (amusingly, the ‘feedback’ button has caused numerous users’ apps to crash when pressed) to sending DMs to the wrong person, or even to a server. 

While the ‘new’ UI has been available for a number of months, discord has always included the option to instead use the old one for users who prefer it. Removing that option was an unfortunate sign in the decline in quality of the developers’ responses to user feedback, and is a major blight on what has otherwise been an amazing app up until this point.",1,207,:3 chloe,1
au,Australia,12042716519,2024-12-08T23:31:45-07:00,It's fine,"I've been using discord for a few years now, but all the recent changes have been generally for the worse. 
The major user-interface change for the phone app version is one of my major gripes, it feels like a copy-paste from messenger but somehow even worse. The older layout that's still on other versions of the platform was a bit confusing to me as a new user but is way more fluid to use than typical messaging app layouts.
Additionally, discord recently lowered the free upload limit to just 10MB, as if most modern files, including a simple screenshot, aren't around 15MB minimum. It feels as if the app is forcing users to pay for nitro, the subscription version of discord, just to use basic features like image/ video share. It really should just compress files instead of demanding you buy nitro.
There's also many persisting bugs like notifications not clearing properly, and sending videos from inside discord (at least on the phone app) occasionally turns them into a useless file link that you can't open by phone. The search-within-chat feature is unusable, and rarely gives you all the messages that actually contain what you're looking for. This also used to function a lot better before the big UI overhaul.

Unless you're getting the app to talk to specific friends/ there's no other options available, I really wouldn't recommend this app. It gets worse with every update.

Tldr: discord just wants your money, and the phone app is the worst version of discord.",2,257.0,Pls read review,0
au,Australia,8455783932,2022-03-14T12:52:54-07:00,"DISCORD IS GREAT, but a recommendation:","Discord is an amazing app, letting me talk to my friends, see my favourite youtuber’s streams, and so on. When I was first introduced to this app, I had to use it by the browser. It worked but I never chatted to any of my friends, so I gave up. Soon about a year later after that, a new friend asks me to get discord. Of course, I got it, as how I had some experience, and soon I got to chat to all of my friends at home! It worked better than messenger, which was useful. 
RECOMMENDATION: 
I would personally recommend letting younger ages use this app, like 12+. Some parents play by the rules, so some kids at maybe 13 can’t get discord, for example, me. I wanted discord when I found out about it, but I had to wait for a year or so to get it. Some kids do already use it, but strict parents wouldn’t allow their kids, so I think it would please children if you had lowered the age restriction.
I also recommend that if you download on an iPad, you can see the compass. I am currently using discord on an iPad, since it has a bigger screen, and I don’t wanna talk to my friends on a PC. I first used iPad for discord, and I’m not seeing the compass that the instructions tell me about. So I have had to use the browser for discord to join special servers. 

Anyways I hope you enjoyed my rating! Of course Discord most likely won’t see it or do it, but it’s just a recommendation!",4,117.1,15_MissedCalls,3
au,Australia,9925231697,2023-05-14T00:51:10-07:00,Remove Clyde auto-ending calls,"Discord has its glitchy moments with notifications, but on the whole is a solid app. However, I absolutely hate the new “feature” which means private calls on mobile are automatically ended after three minutes if one person leaves. I rely on discord to call my long distance partner and we love falling asleep with each other on the call and checking in with each other throughout the day/night as the other person sleeps to see if they’re okay. It was so disheartening the first time we discovered that Clyde had disconnected the call after three minutes, meaning we couldn’t check on each other without waking the other person up and making a new call. 

I understand that the idea behind it is the save data/bandwidth, but that’s for me to manage, not discord. 

I’m really disappointed that this has been added and think it should be at least a toggle button where you can disable Clyde from auto-ending private calls on both PC and mobile. It’s up to me to manage how I spend my time on the app, not discord to decide for me.",1,177.1,Meerzy,1
au,Australia,14336590287,2026-07-22T18:50:08-07:00,Good app but HORRIBLE customer service,"I have spent money on this app for a little while now to buy things for my friends and myself, and every once in a while I run into a complication. Almost 2 years ago I spent money and due to a glitch in THEIR system I lost the money and was given zero and told “ stop spamming” their email. Fast forward to almost 2 years later, for some reason they have set my account as based in Singapore, even though it’s not, I am unable to make any purchases, I have already contacted customer support and gotten a reply to which was no help because they were telling me to do something that I had googled myself. If you’re going to get this app enjoy it without spending money because the customer service is horrible, it is the worst customer service I have ever had, just enjoy this app without the perks that are locked behind pay walls to enjoy because they are greedy and can’t give proper customer service service.",3,338.0,RalseiUnicorn72,0
