au,Australia,9833932478,2023-04-17T22:49:50-07:00,Potentially god tier app let down by lack of support,"Still the best voice and video chat around, and an unavoidable app if you game with other people. Still, support is lacking. Support seems to be staffed primarily by robots who don’t read your replies or even the original problem report. Reported bugs never get fixed, even after providing mountains of evidence and even, in some cases, telling them how to fix it. Dev team more interested in shiny new features than making the stuff they already have perfect before moving onto the next shiny thing. Basically all the hallmarks of a company driven by something like scrum, which you can’t spell without “scum”.

Hopefully with the new advances in AI, Discord will finally be able to get some decent support staff, even if they’re not human.",4,173.0,Red Curry Ninja,0
au,Australia,10887727783,2024-01-31T23:46:25-07:00,Revert recent updates,"Discord mobile used to be super easy and convenient to use. Every recent update has completely spat on that. Want to quickly send or take a photo? It now takes twice as long. Want to check your DMs? It’s no longer as easy as seeing it and pressing it, you have to go to a whole different tab and then looks for the right DM. Every single thing you might want to do on this app is now made more difficult, except for maybe creating a thread (which is something I very rarely do, and did not need easier access to). I don’t see the point of changing an app that previously worked really well and felt good to use, especially when none of the changes have been good. Most interesting or positive changes require money to use them to their fullest extent (soundboards, profile banners etc). Stop changing the app just for the sake of it. I do not know a single person who has enjoyed these changes.",1,214.0,Aurora Bailey,0
au,Australia,13509770148,2025-12-13T10:55:26-07:00,Terribly glitchy and buggy,"I would have loved to give discord a 5 star review, however as of the recent 308.1 update i’ve experienced so many bugs while using discord mobile. 1, when the person im calling used videocall or shares their screen it caused the app to run on a choppy 2 frames per second. 2, the audio keeps switching rapidly between bluetooth and speaker. 3, everytime im on call and i leave the discord app then get on the discord app, it disconnects my bluetooth headphones and i have to wait a couple minutes for discord to reconnect with my bluetooth headphones.

EDIT: after messing around for a bit i realised the issue. When i videocall without my bluetooth headphones, sony WH520, everything works perfectly fine. However as soon as its connected, it turns the discord app really choppy and laggy at 2 frames per second. It turns out the issue may have to do with bluetooth.",2,308.1,Ziniscool,0
au,Australia,8187909748,2021-12-31T03:02:58-07:00,Perfectè,"Discord is a reliable source where I can create or join multiple different servers, ranging from different varieties in genre, theme and people!
I usually use it for the purpose of speaking with my friends, and sometimes joining casual roleplay groups to do what I do best. You can upload pictures, write pretty big paragraphs and design your profile and own servers!
There’s only one reason why I should rate it a 4, but since it isn’t the apps fault, I won’t!
Sometimes the community can get a bit wild.
By this I mean that it can range from sending random DMs trying to convince somebody who might be 12 to have, well, the adult naughtys, all the way to simple bullying.
I have, of course, never gone to any servers that involve this, but I warn anybody who wants to download Discord, or has it;
Do not enter any servers involving things like racism, general rudeness, online dating (can get super serious) or anything that just seems unnaturally strange to you.
Also random DMs. Avoid those.
Discord is the perfect app to download to chat with people you know or people you feel safe with, but be careful of the community..
some people are lurking..",5,106.0,#BoscoBurgher,0
au,Australia,5282221551,2019-12-16T22:33:50-07:00,"It's Great, But...","Nitro. No, no, before you 'ugh' at me, call me 'cheap' and say the creator is trying to make money, wait.
