au,Australia,8228340936,2022-01-11T03:40:59-07:00,Discord Nitro,"I have enjoyed Discord for a long time now but why would you add nitro just so people get extra things while just chatting? Like just buy nitro to join 100 more extra servers or buy nitro just to use different avatar pictures in servers. I think it is really stupid. I feel like Discord is a pay to get things. Pay for just a texting app? I mean the app is really fun and great but the idea of nitro is over the top. I just want to enjoy Discord. I don’t want to pay just to enjoy Discord more. Sorry if I sound mad I just don’t like the feature. Please reply as soon as you can. Also when I write on mobile my about me, it doesn’t say how many characters to type I have left or any other writing fields.",5,106.0,The Cool and Extreme Gamer,0
au,Australia,13895078624,2026-03-27T22:27:33-07:00,When Discord Support Doesn’t Help,"When I first got Discord, I genuinely loved it. It felt like an amazing place to connect with friends, join communities, and have fun conversations. Everything about it seemed easy, welcoming, and enjoyable, and I spent a lot of time on the platform because of how much I liked it.

But over time, my experience has completely changed. Now, Discord feels frustrating and disappointing. The biggest issue was when my account got hacked, which was honestly stressful and upsetting. I lost access and felt like my privacy and security had been completely violated.

What made things worse was how the situation was handled when I tried to get help. I reached out to moderators hoping for support or at least some guidance, but instead of actually helping me resolve the issue, they just told me to submit a request. That process feels incredibly unhelpful and impersonal. It doesn’t give any immediate support, and it feels like your problem just gets pushed into a queue where nothing actually happens for a long time—if anything happens at all.

From my experience, making a request feels like shouting into the void. There’s no real reassurance, no clear timeline, and no guarantee that your issue will even be properly looked at. When you’re dealing with something serious like a hacked account, being told to just “make a request” feels dismissive and frustrating, especially when you’re already stressed and need urgent help.

Overall, the whole experience left me feeling let down. A platform I used to enjoy and trust now feels unreliable, especially when it comes to handling serious issues like account security and user support.",1,321.0,A.S.I.Y.A.B,1
