au,Australia,9949871753,2023-05-21T03:18:50-07:00,Just One Problem,"I love this app and have been using it for couple years now. Recently on a server I have to do a lot of trading, which means I have to directly message (dm) people for trading offers, but if I dm too many people, it gives me a couple human verify checks, which is fine. But what I don’t like is when I have to wait a couple minutes, bc I’m directly messaging too many people, tho I kinda need to in order to not miss out on any deals and always try to offer when I can. I don’t see why it would do this, bc I only can think of maybe bc of spamming, tho the user could just block me or discord can keep do human verify checks instead tbh.",5,178.0,#WhatsUpBoi,0
au,Australia,7365174664,2021-05-20T04:34:18-07:00,"New “blurple” too saturated, causes eye strain","So I love discord, and I have for ages, but this new update really severely strains my eyes. I struggle with retinal ghosts from really bright colours, and now discord causes the same when it never used to. The hyper-saturation is glaring, and stands out way too much compared to dark mode, or even light mode. I know others have accessibility issues with the new font for example, but the eye strain from the new colour within the app is really too much. The new message notification bar, the message send button, the DM button, they’re all now a new glaring saturation that hurts my eyes even looking at it for a few seconds. I would appreciate an option to revert back to the previous blue, even just within the app, and would change my rating if this happened.",3,74.0,lukadolphin_,2
au,Australia,7291939133,2021-05-02T23:16:35-07:00,Switch accounts,"I first started using discord because I wanted to text my friend. We did try other platforms but discord suited us the best. First I was just using it to text my friend but then when I got used to it, I created my own server which allowed me to get many friends. I love how we can control the servers, make roles and stuff. This app is absolutely amazing. 

