Please consider this, thank you!",4,71.0,Samita Upadhyaya,0
au,Australia,11044933687,2024-03-14T16:00:27-07:00,New discord layout for phone,"This layout is the absolute worst thing to happen to the discord app. On video call, I can barely see each others faces. Before I could see us both, no problem. Now they’re in these little squares on the screen and it’s really annoying when I’m trying to show something and have to full screen my camera so i know i’m showing it properly and instead of focusing on their camera. Also, video doesn’t stay up when you minimise the app anymore. This update is extremely frustrating and I hate it. I’m sure a lot of people feel this way, my boyfriend included. Also not having a friends list as a tab anymore or a search bar. Please change it back. I will change my review when this issue is fixed. For now I am forced to leave 1 star. Edit. No the app is not out of date, your phone UI is absolute garbage. Unhelpful response.",1,220.0,Mewziez,0
au,Australia,5802730039,2020-04-12T15:49:00-07:00,Definitely worth your time,"Discord is a great app. If you’re bored in quarantine, or whenever, it’s really fun to hang out with your friends without the mics cutting out, the audio is really good, and the camera during video calls is really nice. Servers really connect people and i think it’s one of the best things about discord. And if you don’t know what discord is, definitely get the app, it’s really nice and, well, addicting. This is not your ordinary social media platform. This is much better. Even if you aren’t a gamer, it’s so fun to just be with your friends, i definitely recommend this over Skype, teamspeak, facetime, or whatever you use, i guarantee discord will make you regret using those apps all those years.",5,16.0,CJaBlaze,1
au,Australia,12046849367,2024-12-10T03:22:30-07:00,𝓅𝓇ℯ𝓉𝓉𝓎 𝑔ℴℴ𝒹,"With discord, there’s a lot of good thing to do. A good way to chat with friends, built in silly games to play, a lot of good stuff. But , along that discord is very money hungry, without nitro, you can’t send a video longer than 1 minute. Also with the perks of having “moving emojis” a cool custom banner and stuff. That should just be without nitro to be honest. Also the TikTok of discord needs to post more about how to work servers, Becuase when I started discord it took me SOO LONG to figure out how to actually do easy stuff on servers. But those are just the cons, there’s a few more pros, discord is good quality call quality and is really good. Even with my friends with uh.. horrid mics.",5,258.0,aramdomnameidk,0
au,Australia,8108999499,2021-12-08T11:10:25-07:00,It’s super good with one tiny problem-,"So I’ve been using discord for a really long time now, and I’ve never had any previous trouble with other then like update issues. But the other day while I was talking to someone my messages would suddenly stop sending, and when I checked their profile it said that I unfriended then when I hadn’t? And another one of our friends said that I had blocked them when I know that I most definitely didn’t? So, I tried seeing if discord would fix itself overnight but it didn’t. So I’m trying to un-install it and then install it again and see if that work but if it does that means I have to make a whole new account, this meaning I’d lose all my friends and servers.",4,104.0,Nyx_Vex,0
au,Australia,6866580677,2021-01-13T15:45:59-07:00,Great app but no accessibility features,I have only just started using Discord but it is already my favourite app for talking to friends I am one of a few blind users who have been using the app to talk about some of our favourite games and even to play multiplayer on them when we’re not on the same network I am using a screen reader called voice-over and I also use another screen reader on Windows called jaws if you could optimise both the mobile app and the windows addition to run with screen readers that would be amazing until then the app is on usable to me and my friends also if you could simplify the layout a little bit that would be one of the first big steps towards optimisation thank you for reading my slightly long winded review and please take my ideas into consideration,3,56.0,shameru,1
au,Australia,6274829580,2020-08-03T05:31:46-07:00,Amazing!,"Firstly, I just want to say I love this app! It’s so handy and unlike Apple text messages, it uses less storage. But since I’m on mobile I have a few problems that I’d like to address. 

1. How come there’s no screen share on mobile? It’s okay if you can’t, but I’m quite curious as to why you can’t do this. Are phones and tablets just not fast enough and it might crash?
2. Again, mobile is missing something PC has. Why is there no noise suppression on iPad? I saw on phone they added some cool stuff like a phone symbol next to the avatar and background noise suppression. But iPad is yet to have these. Is it you or have I not updated it? 
3. This one is for laptops instead but it’s still worth mentioning. When I was using a laptop, I noticed that there’s lots of scroll sliders on the side (thanks for that). But There’s none for the server list. It was quite annoying when I’d try to scroll and I’d have to use the scroll click and be careful not to click the server. Please add one if you can. I get if it’s too tight but it’s wonderful! 
That’s all! Please keep working on your beautiful app!",5,32.0,ALT_Rag3,0
au,Australia,7321295253,2021-05-10T05:19:03-07:00,I love it but..,"Can I just say, I absolutely love this app and have been using it for over 2 years. I’m in many many servers and hold many roles as moderator. While I do love the app, the thing I find missing the most is coloured text for the mobile version. For whatever reason, you can’t read coloured text in the mobile version nor do the codes work correctly and show you colour. This is a disappointment as I love coloured text but don’t always have access to my laptop. 
If you could please take this under consideration and maybe create an update in the future to accommodate coloured text. It would be the highlight of my year.",5,72.0,jinxarcher,0
au,Australia,7507929525,2021-06-26T05:31:49-07:00,Discord Disabled My Account,"I joined discord in 2019 and have been a part of the community for over 2 years. I purchased several subscriptions such as nitro and server boosting, however when my account was disabled, I was still subscribed to these services. 
I’m unsure why my account was disabled in the first place, and when trying to contact the discord support team I received an automated reply and then never heard from them again. 
Now I am unable to use the platform, and cannot access my servers I spent hours on. 
Discord does not cancel the subscriptions if your account is disabled. If you cannot get into your account then you cannot cancel them. You need to use a third party app to cancel the subscriptions which took me ages to figure out. 
My account was disabled without any notice, and I cannot get it back. Be aware of everything you do, Discord is full of toxic communities.",1,80.0,Zac#6969,0
au,Australia,9937543982,2023-05-17T14:33:08-07:00,Make auto disconnect on private calls optional,"I’ve been a discord user for years and have always loved the app, but forcing auto disconnect after being alone in a call for 3 minutes without even warning us in the what’s new page and leaving people to find out by themselves total bull, I am the type on person who likes to sleep on call and this just made it so if my device dies or something I can’t rejoin the call in the morning because it would’ve disconnected. And the disconnect sound is so when I leave for work or school in the morning the sound of the call disconnecting after 3 minutes wakes up the person I call with. I understand the feature and why you would implement it but it should be optional, Youve gotten hundreds on complaints about this so please hurry up and fix it. It’s out internet let us do what we want with it.",1,178.0,KitKat3350,2
au,Australia,4741528091,2019-09-07T03:33:32-07:00,One glitch that I have now,"I RLLY love this app so much however, now I have a glitch I can’t get rid of on mobile. It all started a few hours ago when everytime I was in a priv call, it would disconnect me from the call entirely after 5 seconds (as in it makes me leave the call but everything else is fine). It’s been happening and I don’t know how to fix it. It’s so annoying too so now I have to use my computer for it. Can u guys pls fix this glitch? Cause it’s annoying getting yourself removed from the call every 5 seconds. I don’t know whether it affects public voice chats tho but I think it does too. Just please fix this for mobile. On pc my disc is fine",5,3.1.1,Bubbleninegamer21,2
au,Australia,7880617955,2021-10-05T05:16:38-07:00,Best socialising app I’ve had,"This is easily one the best app for socialising I’ve come across because it’s simple to use to begin with but can be also quite advanced if the user wants better a experience. As well as the previous point, many other small features make it great e.g deleting a message deletes from both the sender and receiver and a filter to make it easy to find older or specific messages. Occasionally you’ll meet a not-so-child-friendly person except in general the community is great. Almost everyone I know uses it and is my primary online socialising and messaging app. I strongly recommend Discord to pretty much anyone.",5,94.0,IAmBest.01,0
au,Australia,7749649933,2021-08-29T17:11:59-07:00,BEST APP EVER HAS COOL THINGS OTHERS DO NOT,"I love using discord for everything with my friends. This app has so many cool features such as screen sharing on calls and I do know that zoom has this too except discord’s calls or video chats don’t randomly end. Unlike a few  other apps this app does not make you do any subscription unless there is something you want to do and the subscriptions or in app purchases don’t cost a crazy amount of money, they are just right. I would totally recommend this app to others and if you don’t want to be seen by random people that okay you don’t have to but if you want to you can and that’s why I love this app!",5,88.2,mdur5677,0
au,Australia,11223120434,2024-05-02T01:15:00-07:00,Mobile Sever Shop,"Discord is a great app and I highly recommend it to everyone who plays video games with a group of friends, just one problem.

