au,Australia,6955763461,2021-02-04T22:24:54-07:00,kinda went downhill not gonna lie....,"alright! so i was introduced to discord almost three, four years ago. it's changed my life and introduced me to a bunch of cool folks. now it's mostly my go-to for contacting people / keeping in touch with my friends. it's a great app, would highkey recommend... if you have a laptop.

i will say that it's a good app. but anyone with working eyes can tell it was not optimized for mobile. and that's where the problems start.

it's slow and buggy as hell on my iphone, inputs take 5 million years to get through (keep in mind that i've gone through several routers already, it did not fix anything) and some messages will glitch out and not appear. the list of bugs go on and on, because apparently even with the bug fixes my iphone keeps having issues with sending messages, getting chat to load-- and god forbid i bring up calling on mobile. it's horrible because the INSTANT i leave the app to get a screenshot or something the whole call crashes and i have to reload, which takes a horrendously long time. 

sometimes ill get stuck on the call screen and be unable to do anything for upwards of 10-20 minutes. it just freezes and more often than not it crashes completely, which is... not ideal, seeing as i can't haul around my bulky pc everywhere i go. 

i have thought that maybe it was an issue with my phone. it is possible, with this clunky piece of junk. but i've seen discord crash on my friends' phones as well, though usually nowhere as bad as what i'm experiencing. 

if it's any consolation, the app isn't as bad on ipad, though... the voice chat problems are still present, especially in big group calls. and the moment you close the app it crashes too. 

if these problems get fixed that would be rad! thank you :D",2,59.0,cineavi,0
au,Australia,13923221608,2026-04-04T16:12:10-07:00,Great App! I have a suggestion for an idea to implement that would be very useful.,"Would it be possible to add custom gif folders, this would make sorting our favourite gifs way easier. I myself have lots of favourite gifs which I use for different replies and emotions etc and after awhile, the amount of gifs stack up which can make it very annoying to reply to someone faster as I have to search for the right gif to use. However, if we had the option to sort our gifs into custom folders, ie; funny, silly, crazy, serious etc, we would be able to find the right gifs for the right occasion.",5,322.0,Kai ohilo,0
au,Australia,9693772640,2023-03-08T18:27:53-07:00,Authenticator,"I can’t replace my Authenticator codes/app, due to you’s promoting “extra security” for using it, as every site/company/app etc. nowadays. Yet every other place will allow you to retrieve your access to your Authenticator by being able to disable and re-enable it for you if you’ve had some sort of issue. Like myself, I had a phone which was on a plan, I’ve returned the phone at the end of the plans period I lost the app and codes, now I’m told “we can’t get it back for you, you’ll have to make a new account” basically… it automatically logs me out on my phone overtime of not using it, idk why, I literally signed in twice now, used two back-up codes about to be my third, so I’m being forced to use up all my back-up codes within the next year I assume it’s been that constant, then make a new account eventually? Bert, very poor resolution.",1,168.0,ImJaiden,0
au,Australia,8828590446,2022-07-01T00:52:20-07:00,Good and bad things,"Dear Discord,
