au,Australia,10665490634,2023-12-06T19:53:18-07:00,New UI :(,"The new UI places private messages in the bottom menu on the screen instead of above servers — this majorly lowers visibility and leads to missing notifications. I didn’t realise I had messages for a while because of this :(

It has also changed to swipe-to-reply to messages in chats, which has replaced the prior slide ability to view online server members. This option is now hidden behind two steps, and doesn’t even grey-out offline members. 

The search function has also changed now: when it used to be a server-wide search is now on a single channel basis, meaning if you are looking for something in particular but don’t know where it is, it is now an entire ordeal to find

Overall, these new features drastically lower the usability of the app and are inefficient; especially when long-time users have everything down by muscle memory. 

(To note: I also got warning of this UI update from a friend and turned off auto app updates in preparation only to find the change happened anyway. Not happy)",2,207,skarmoree,0
au,Australia,10665031476,2023-12-06T16:26:52-07:00,Don’t update to the latest update.,"I use discord daily, and love it to the point I bought nitro. However the latest update has completely changed the whole app look and function to the point where I cannot use it the way I have been for the last five years. 

It is entirely unoptimised for people who get a lot of notifications, and for mobile app users a lot of the previous well loved functions and appearance have been either removed or replaced with new icons and features that do barely a fraction of what the old ones could do. 

If you haven’t had the new update yet, do not download it.",3,207,smiley5494,0
au,Australia,10455010355,2023-10-09T01:52:18-07:00,"Competent apps have recovery options, but not this one","App has no option to change email address if you have lost access to your email account (the provider I used when I signed up to discord years ago no longer exists, so it simply isn’t possible to regain access to the email - I explained this in my support request and the agent simply suggested I contact the email provider - gee, thanks for taking the time to read my short email). 

 The only advice given was to create a new account. Gee, thanks. I know the password, I have a mobile as a contact point and friends who could confirm my identity- my other apps have these options for account recovery, just not this one one. 

I guess the name of the app now makes sense.  

Other than that what started off as a nice and simple chat app has become a hodge-podge mess of monetising options that are constantly pushed in your way. I fully support making money to run your app, but HOW you go about it really matters.

Edit: what a GrEaT developer response. Another example of well they read 🙄",2,198.1,RedFinito,0
